\par\par \b \uc2 Potential  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Forex Interventions \highlight\uc2  Unlikely to Halt Yen's Slide -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 2022\par 12:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1051 GMT - The Japanese yen could extend its recent losses even if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , ING analysts say in a note. Remarks by Japan's finance minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  on Wednesday describing the yen's sharp depreciation as "very problematic" suggest authorities have moved into the stage of heightened surveillance of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which normally precedes \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the analysts say. "However, unless the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to hike rates, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can only temporarily interrupt what should be a grind higher in USD/JPY this summer," they say. USD/JPY could rise to 130, according to the analysts. USD/JPY falls 0.2% to 125.316 after hitting a 20-year high of 126.285 on Wednesday, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2  . (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1021 GMT - The cost of insuring against European junk-bond defaults is unchanged from the previous day's close at a one-month high, ahead of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's interest-rate decision later Thursday. The iTraxx Europe Crossover index, which tracks euro high-yield credit default swaps, trades flat at 378 basis points from Wednesday, \uc2 IHS Markit\uc2  data shows. Stock markets also trade steady, with the pan-continental Stoxx Europe 600 up less than 0.1%. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 1009 GMT - Sterling could fall if the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  maintains its gradual approach to raising interest rates due to caution about the U.K.'s economic prospects, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says. In view of soaring U.K. inflation, the \uc2 BOE\uc2  will need to start sounding more "restrictive" about policy soon, \uc2 Commerzbank\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst \uc2 Antje Praefcke\uc2  says in a note. "Otherwise, it faces the risk of the market fearing that it could drop behind the curve or that it might be afraid of stagflation [weak growth combined with high inflation]," she says. "Both could put pressure on sterling, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that might have peaked." GBP/USD rises 0.3% to 1.3141 after earlier reaching a one-week high of 1.3148 as the dollar falls, but EUR/GBP trades flat at 0.8308.(renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0933 GMT - Firms operating in consumer services, energy and natural resources struggled the most globally to service their debt burdens in 2021, says S&P Global Ratings in a report. In 2021, "defaults fell across nearly every sector, but consumer services and energy and natural resources led the tally for the seventh year in a row," says the rating agency. Global defaults in consumer services, energy and natural resources accounted for about 40% of the total. This is as the S&P Global Ratings global speculative-grade corporate default rate fell below 2% for only the eighth time in the past 41 years in 2021, to 1.7%, it says. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0925 GMT - European markets are mostly steady ahead of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's interest-rate decision later. The Stoxx Europe 600 and Germany's DAX are flat, France's CAC 40 rises 0.1%, though the FTSE 100 falls 0.1% as tobacco and utility stocks drop. Brent crude falls 0.6% to around $108.20 a barrel. IG futures data show the Dow opening at 34,573, versus Wednesday's close of 34,564. "Thursday's big event is the \uc2 ECB\uc2  decision, which isn't expected to result in any changes in policy, though comments regarding the outlook for inflation and interest rates will be as closely watched as ever," IG analysts say. (philip.waller@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0922 GMT - The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably won't meet the market's expectations for a "hawkish tilt" in signalling faster policy tightening at Thursday's meeting, potentially weakening the euro, ING says. Uncertainty over the economic implications of the Ukraine war will encourage policymakers to keep their options open, ING analysts say. That means along with a well-telegraphed openness towards a 2022 interest rate increase, the \uc2 ECB\uc2  will reiterate that rates won't rise until after quantitative easing ends while leaving its asset purchase schedule unchanged, they say. "This may translate into a weaker euro, which is still looking at an unsupportive external environment due to uncertainty around the French elections and the Russia-Ukraine conflict." EUR/USD could fall to 1.0800 from 1.0913 currently, they say. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0905 GMT - The euro will weaken if the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't raise interest rates soon to tackle accelerating inflation, \uc2 Swissquote Bank\uc2  analyst Ipek Ozkardeskaya says. The \uc2 ECB\uc2  must raise rates by the end of summer, even though inflation is caused by supply side problems that can't be effectively addressed by restricting demand, she says in a note. "If the \uc2 ECB\uc2  doesn't act, the tighter monetary policy from other major central banks will send the value of euro crushing, which would add an additional pressure on inflation." EUR/USD could rise above 1.10 if the \uc2 ECB\uc2  signals imminent policy tightening at Thursday's meeting but a soft response could send it below 1.08, she says. EUR/USD trades at 1.0908. The \uc2 ECB\uc2  's decision is at 1145 GMT. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0901 GMT - The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will need to signal that it's planning to raise interest rates sooner than previously indicated at Thursday's meeting to reverse the euro's recent weakening trend, \uc2 MUFG Bank\uc2  says. The \uc2 ECB\uc2  is in an increasingly challenging position when setting policy as risks to Europe's economic growth continue to build due to the Ukraine war, China's ongoing coronavirus disruptions and worries about a potential victory for far-right candidate \uc2 Marine Le Pen\uc2  in the French presidential election, \uc2 MUFG\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst \uc2 Lee Hardman\uc2  says in note. "These downside growth risks have all been weighing on the euro at the start of this month." The \uc2 ECB\uc2  's decision is at 1145 GMT followed by a press conference at 1230 GMT. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0857 GMT - A stronger-than-expected increase in Swedish inflation in March is likely to give more ammunition to the hawks in the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  , says \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  . "The increase in headline CPIF inflation in March, from 4.5% in February to 6.1%, lifted the rate to its highest level since December 1991 and to more than triple the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  's 2.0% target." Looking ahead, the war in Ukraine has caused renewed upward pressure on energy prices and exacerbated global supply-demand imbalances, while the recent depreciation of the krona is likely to feed into higher imported goods inflation, it says. "Against this backdrop, we think headline CPIF inflation will stay above 2% for some time...the chance of a repo rate hike in 1H is rising." (dominic.chopping@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0855 GMT - Upside surprises in inflation and an uncertain growth outlook due to the war in Ukraine have made the majority of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Governing Council to argue for a "data-dependent and step-by-step approach," says \uc2 Dirk Schumacher\uc2  , head of European macro research at \uc2 Natixis\uc2  . The crucial question for the \uc2 ECB\uc2  's April meeting Thursday is whether the end of net asset purchases under the Asset Purchase Programme will be brought forward, he says, seeing the scope for a nuanced tweak in the \uc2 ECB\uc2  's wording. "While we think it is likely that the [\uc2 ECB\uc2  's] statement will re-confirm the 'third quarter' as the end of net asset purchases, we expect President [Christine] Lagarde to signal that the Governing Council is leaning towards 'early 3Q'," he says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0817 GMT - The S&P Global Ratings global speculative-grade corporate default rate fell below 2% in 2021, representing the eighth time this happened in past 41 years, the rating agency says in a report. The rate stood at 1.7% last year, with the global default tally falling to 72. Of those, 60 were from companies with active ratings at the start of the year versus 226 in 2020, S&P says. "S&P Global Ratings' corporate issuer credit ratings performed very well globally in 2021, with all rated defaulters beginning the year in the 'B' category or lower," it says. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0817 GMT - Global corporate bond downgrades fell in 2021, alongside a decline in the default rate, says S&P Global Ratings in a report. "Corporate downgrades also decreased, outstripped by upgrades by 1.85x," the rating agency says. The downgrade rate fell to its lowest yet, at 5.5%, and last year was the first since 2013 with an upgrade rate above 10%, it says. Still, despite the increase in credit quality relative to 2020, "the ratings distribution among companies we rate remained weak, with 14.5% of ratings at 'B-' or lower as of year-end, up from 7.4% 10 years earlier," says Nick Kraemer, head of S&P Global Ratings Performance Analytics. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 14, 2022 06:52 ET (10:52 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020220414ei4e001f8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
