\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 1-Japan's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  keeps up yield defense, focus on bond-buying schedule\b0\par\par\uc2 466 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par 05:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 BOJ\uc2  offers fixed-rate unlimited bond buying as expected\par \par \uc2 * Markets focusing on \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's April-June buying schedule\par \par \uc2 * Govt official sticks to usual script on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves\par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara and Junko Fujita\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 31 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday offered to buy unlimited amounts of 10-year government bonds for the fourth straight day as part of its aggressive efforts to defend its yield curve against the global tide of higher interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The announcement was expected and in line with the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's earlier pledge to continue with the offer until Thursday, the final day of the first quarter.\par \par \uc2 Investors are focusing on whether the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  could increase the frequency and volume of bond purchases under a second-quarter market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  schedule, slated for release later on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 After falling to as low as 0.210% on Wednesday due to the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yield on the benchmark 10-year Japanese government bond (JGB) yield crept up to 0.225% on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The level was still below the 0.25% implicit cap the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  sets around its 0% target.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  may increase bond buying somewhat in the second quarter, so markets make take a breather after testing the 0.25% cap," said Chotaro Morita, head of Japan rates strategy at \uc2 SMBC Nikko Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The super dovish \uc2 BOJ\uc2  is struggling against the tide of rising global interest rates as central banks elsewhere race to beat accelerating inflation, with the international spike in yields dragging Japan's rates higher.\par \par \uc2 Complicating that challenge for Tokyo policymakers are the rising costs of imports brought by a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and global fallout of the Ukraine war.\par \par \uc2 Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat on Tuesday escalated his warning against sharp yen falls, saying Tokyo and Washington were closely communicating on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues.\par \par \uc2 But policymakers have yet to caution against "one-sided" moves or stress their resolve to take "decisive action," which are phrases markets look out for as a sign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be imminent.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability is important and sharp exchange-rate moves are undesirable," Chief Cabinet Secretary \uc2 Hirokazu Matsuno\uc2  told reporters on Wednesday, repeating the government's recent official line on the weak yen.\par \par \uc2 The yen's fall has inflated already rising raw material costs blamed on the Ukraine crisis, adding pain to households and clouding the outlook for Japan's fragile economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Factory output rose 0.1% in February from the previous month, ata showed on Thursday, posting its first rise in three months but smaller than forecast.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Leika Kihara and Junko Fujita, Additional reporting by Kantaro Komiya and Daniel Leussink Editing by Shri Navaratnam) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-3-31T04:15:05.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220331ei3v00cqd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
