\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Asian markets rally as geopolitical fears ease; Thai cenbank holds rates\b0\par\par\uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par 10:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  holds rate at a record low\par     * Korean won strengthens 0.8% \par     * Malaysian cenbank cuts growth forecast \par     * All regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , stock (ex-Japan) gain\par \par     By Harshita Swaminathan\par     March 30 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and equity markets\par gained on Wednesday as the likelihood of a negotiated resolution\par to the Russia-Ukraine war boosted risk appetite, while\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stood pat on its key interest rate to\par support a pandemic-ravaged economy.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  reduced its growth outlook for 2022\par while saying it expected inflation to come in above the target\par this year before falling back within its 1-3% target range next\par year. \par     The baht and Thai equities inched\par marginally higher after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's much-expected\par decision. \par     "As long as there is no broad inflation pressure, just\par energy and foods prices that rise sharply, I think the MPC will\par feel less concerned about inflationary pressures. So they will\par mainly focus on economic outlook i.e. when Thailand's economy\par will recover from the COVID-19," said Poon Panichpibool, a\par markets strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Krung Thai Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     Late on Tuesday, negotiators from Russia and Ukraine met in\par Istanbul, where Moscow promised to scale back military action\par around Kyiv and another city, and Ukraine proposed adopting a\par neutral status. \par     The positive news sent global markets rallying, and Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and stocks tracked the cues to climb higher. Emerging\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stood to benefit as the U.S. dollar fell on\par shedding some of its safe-haven appeal. \par     "There's certainly not a sense that there's a deal at this\par point in time, but at least there seems to be positive noise,"\par said Mitul Kotecha, senior EM strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     South Korea's won strengthened 0.8% to over a\par one-week high of 1,209.6 to the dollar, and the Indian rupee\par  firmed 0.2%, leading the pack of emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Malaysia's ringgit strengthened 0.3% as investors\par appeared to show scant reaction to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision\par to cut economic growth forecast.  \par     Meanwhile, the yield on two-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  notes briefly\par overtook the yield on the benchmark 10-year overnight, inverting\par the yield curve and again raising fears of a recession.\par  \par     Yields on Singapore's benchmark 10-year bond\par tracked U.S. peers lower, losing 77 basis points to 2.361%.\par Yields in Indonesia moved 3 basis points lower,\par while those in the Philippines were flat. \par     Among equities, Chinese stocks surged 1.7%, set for\par their best day in about two weeks as property firms led the\par gains. \par     Kotecha also attributed some of the strength in equities to\par the global sell-off in bond markets. \par     Stocks in India surged 0.9% while shares in the Philippines\par and Indonesia climbed 0.6% and 0.3%, respectively. \par  \par     HIGHLIGHTS:\par     ** \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yen gains 0.8% as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to help \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakness    \par     ** Debt-embattled Chinese property developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 China\par Evergrande Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  says it will sell a project in\par Hangzhou, China for $575 million to two state-owned firms\par  \par     \par     \par   Asia stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                              \par  at 0659 GMT                                              \par  COUNTRY   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RIC           \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     INDEX    STOCKS  STOCKS\par                        DAILY %  YTD %            DAILY %   YTD %\par  Japan                   +0.75  -5.62            -0.80    -2.66\par  China                   +0.12  -0.02               1.74  -10.44\par  India                   +0.23  -1.94               0.92    0.75\par  Indonesi                +0.13  -0.66               0.31    6.87\par  a                                                        \par  Malaysia                +0.29  -0.86               0.02    1.03\par  Philippi                +0.00  -1.89               0.61    0.50\par  nes                                                      \par  S.Korea                 +0.84  -1.72               0.21   -7.75\par  Singapor                +0.16  -0.38               0.15   10.10\par  e                                                        \par  Taiwan                  +0.78  -2.98               1.09   -2.63\par  Thailand                +0.81  +0.18               0.55    2.49\par  \par     \par \par  (Reporting by Harshita Swaminathan; Editing by Sherry\par Jacob-