\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 3-\uc2 BOJ\uc2  stands its ground on benchmark yield as global rates pressure builds\b0\par\par\uc2 782 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par 09:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Bank ramps up 3-10 year JGB buying in scheduled \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 BOJ\uc2  offers to buy super-long JGBs in emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Says ready to ramp up further buying as needed\par \par \uc2 * Gov Kuroda unfazed at weak yen after meeting PM Kishida\par \par \uc2 * Japan unlikely to buy yen, hike rates -former \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  tsar Shinohara\par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara and Kevin Buckland\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 30 (Reuters) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped up efforts on Wednesday to keep a key bond yield below a red line, offering to buy more government debt, including through ad-hoc purchases, to hold down interest rates against a pull higher by global yields.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes as the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 BOJ\uc2 ) seeks to keep monetary policy ultra-loose, even at the cost of fuelling further falls in the yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which could push up import costs and hurt the economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased purchases of Japanese government bonds (JGB) with maturities of three to 10 years, and offered to buy super-long bonds in unscheduled, emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Combined, the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  offered to buy more than 2 trillion yen ($16.40 billion) worth of JGBs on Wednesday, in addition to separate offers for unlimited purchases of 10-year JGBs at a fixed rate of 0.25%.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  is trying to strengthen its message to the market, that it's strongly committed to keeping financial conditions in Japan very accommodative and won't accept those kinds of higher long-term bond yields," said Masayuki Kichikawa, chief macro strategist at Sumitomo Mitsui Asset Management.\par \par \uc2 "We need to remember the official \uc2 BOJ\uc2  target is 0% for the 10-year JGB, not 25 basis points."\par \par \uc2 The move bolsters the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the bond market unveiled on Monday, when it pledged to buy unlimited amounts of 10-year bonds at 0.25% until Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the benchmark 10-year JGBs retreated on Wednesday from a more than six-year peak hit earlier in the week, falling 3.0 basis points to 0.215%.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's emergency offer to buy super-long bonds also drove down yields on longer-dated maturities. The 20-year JGB yield lost 8.5 basis points to 0.73% and the 30-year JGB yield was down 10 basis points at 0.970%.\par \par \uc2 "We decided to take the step because the entire yield curve was under strong upward pressure, heightening the risk of the 10-year yield exceeding our upper limit," a \uc2 BOJ\uc2  official told Reuters about Wednesday's move.\par \par \uc2 WEAK YEN DILEMMA\par \par \uc2 The super dovish \uc2 BOJ\uc2  is struggling against the tide of rising global interest rates as central banks elsewhere race to beat accelerating inflation, with the international spike in yields dragging Japan's yields higher.\par \par \uc2 Complicating that challenge for Tokyo policymakers are the rising costs of imports brought by a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and global fallout of the Ukraine war.\par \par \uc2 BOJ\uc2  Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  appeared unfazed over the yen's fall, saying the move was driven partly by Japanese firms' dollar buying to pay energy bills.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is having a direct effect on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves," Kuroda told reporters after meeting Prime Minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 . "We didn't discuss anything in particular on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves."\par \par \uc2 Despite increasing official jawboning over the yen's fall, Japanese authorities are unlikely to opt for direct yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or raise the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's yield targets to strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said former top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Naoyuki Shinohara.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's position appears to be that a weak yen is good for the economy," Shinohara told Reuters. "It probably doesn't see the yen's current levels as dangerous."\par \par \uc2 Markets will watch for the release of the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's bond-buying schedule for the April-June quarter, set for 5 p.m. on Thursday (0800GMT), to seek any signs of additional purchases.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  will increase the number of auction dates and the amount of outright JGB purchases as needed, taking account of market conditions," the bank said in announcing Wednesday's plan to ramp up bond buying.\par \par \uc2 Under yield curve control, the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  sets its short-term rate target at -0.1% and that for the 10-year JGB yield around 0%.\par \par \uc2 Its current guidance is to allow the 10-year yield to move flexibly, as long as it is below an implicit 0.25% ceiling set around the target. ($1=121.9300 yen) (Reporting by Leika Kihara and Kevin Buckland; Additional reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto, Takahiko Wada, Kantaro Komiya, Daniel Leussink and Daiki Iga; Editing by Sam Holmes and Bradley Perrett) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-3-30T08:55:22.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220330ei3u00bq9\par }\pag