\par\par \b \uc2 Treasury Yields Rise Ahead of Fed Rate Moves -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par 14:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0826 ET - Treasury yields rise across the board while the 2y-10y curve nears an inversion many see as an indicator of upcoming recession. The 10-year yield rises to 2.498% from 2.476% Monday and the two-year hits 2.415% from 2.340%. \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  economists say about the yield curve that "we have multiple recessionary signals starting or continuing to flash," noting that the 2y-10y segment "has inverted prior to every one of the last 10 US recessions." \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  says markets are pricing a pace of Fed rate increases that, if realised would be "the largest move tighter in a calendar year since 1994." (paulo.trevisani@wsj.com; @ptrevisani)\par \par \uc2 0816 ET - Bitcoin could extend its appreciation as data from on-chain analytics firm Glassnode show 60% of the cryptocurrency's supply hasn't moved for at least one year, digital asset broker GlobalBlock says. "The only other time the percentage of bitcoin's supply hadn't moved in over a year was September 2020, which lead to a 500% move in price over the following eight months," GlobalBlock says. Another positive development for bitcoin is a report from \uc2 Coinshares\uc2  on Monday that revealed investment flows into crypto funds reached the highest level since December, the broker says. Bitcoin rises 1.1% to $47,677, according to CoinDesk. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0805 ET - \uc2 J.P.Morgan\uc2  's rates strategists recommend investors to enter long in 30-year Belgian government bonds, or OLOs, versus French OAT peers, to benefit from attractive valuations and limited supply pressures, they say. The strategists add that longer-dated Belgian government bonds are still trading in the upper-end of their past 12-month trading range versus France. This contrast the pattern in 10-year and shorter-dated OLOs which trade flat to below equivalent French OAT yields. "We find 10Y+ OLOs trading at 8bp or more pick-up over similar maturity OATs excessive and hard to justify on fundamentals, liquidity or supply considerations," \uc2 JPM\uc2  's strategists add. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0729 ET - The euro rises on optimism over Russia-Ukraine peace talks on Tuesday but the gains are likely to remain limited, ActivTrades says. A positive outcome from the talks would be a ceasefire and potentially an agreement to end hostilities, ActivTrades says. "However, such an outcome is far from guaranteed and therefore today's gains must not be taken as the beginning of a recovery, with the euro likely to remain squeezed by the economic impact of the Russian-Ukrainian war, high inflation and the comparatively dovish stance of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  , in relation to that of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and other major central banks." EUR/USD rises to a one-week high of 1.1057, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2  . (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0716 ET - Indications that Japan will take action to curb yen volatility could offer the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  some support but that will play second fiddle to moves in Japanese government bond yields, ING says. "The yen remains highly vulnerable as long as bond yields continue to press higher--and a return to [USD/JPY] 125 today is not off the charts," ING analysts say. Japan's 10-year yield remains dangerously close to the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  's 0.25% target despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bond market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they say. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat, Masato Kanda, on Tuesday said Japan and the U.S. agreed communicate closely on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues. USD/JPY falls 0.2% to 123.537 after hitting its highest level since August 2015 at 125.036 on Monday. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0637 ET - The cost of insuring against European junk bond defaults fall sharply Tuesday as investors remain optimistic amid Ukraine-Russia peace talks in Turkey. The iTraxx Europe Crossover index, which tracks euro high-yield credit default swaps, falls 15 basis points to a seven-day low of 346 bps in early trading from Monday's close, \uc2 IHS Markit\uc2  data shows." A sense of positivity returned to financial markets as the prospects of more ceasefire talks between Russia and Ukraine soothed investor jitters," FXTM says. Stock markets continue to rise, with the pan-continental Stoxx Europe 600 jumping 1.3% and S&P 500 futures up 0.3%. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0609 ET - With eurozone inflation set to average around 6% this year, \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  expects aggregate real household incomes to fall by about 1.5%. The U.K. economic-research firm has reduced its eurozone household spending forecast for this year from 5.5% to 4.0%. "The impact on consumption will be cushioned to some extent by fiscal support and, to a greater extent, by a decline in the saving rate," \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  says. This should help the economy avoid a recession but \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  still thinks that GDP growth will be weaker than either consensus or \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expectations this year, forecasting growth of only 2.8%. (maria.martinez@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0606 ET - \uc2 Barclays\uc2  faces reputation issues following a bond blunder, says \uc2 Hargreaves Lansdown\uc2  . The British bank said it issued more securities than it had registered for sale in the U.S., meaning it will have to repurchase the affected bonds at their original price, taking a loss of GBP450 million. "This is a highly embarrassing turn of events for \uc2 Barclays\uc2  ," HL says, adding that stock investors are clearly irked about the mismanagement of the structured product sales and the quick fire purchase, which sees the bank nursing a heavy loss. The blunder has also delayed the bumper GBP1 billion share buy back, adding toshareholders' angst, HL says. Still, underlying performance of the business is positive, and the bank is well capitalised, with a CET1 radio higher than the regulatory minimum, it adds. \uc2 Barclays\uc2  ' shares fall 3.3%. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0535 ET - The U.K. yield curve has flattened, suggesting investors are concerned about economic growth, says \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  . "The fact that the gilt curve flattened despite this pricing out of rate hikes is noteworthy, as it points to the market focusing upon the scale of the headwinds facing the U.K. economy rather than the modest reduction in rate hike expectations," \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  analysts say. A more cautious tone from the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  at its March 17 meeting, due to a looming squeeze on real household incomes, led investors to unwind bets that interest rates could rise more aggressively, even by 50 basis points, in coming meetings. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0535 ET - Government bond issuance in the eurozone is expected to drop slightly in 2Q compared with 1Q but the economic impact of the Ukraine war represents uncertainty for national budgets, Elmar Voelker, senior fixed income analyst at LBBW, says in a note. "The possible negative impact of the war in Ukraine on the budget situation of the countries is a major unknown," he says. LBBW expects gross government bond issuance of eurozone countries to ease by 3% to around EUR325 billion in 2Q from 1Q. LBBW is of the view that crisis-related additional financing requirements will initially be covered primarily by higher money market issuance, but Voelker says there is a considerable upside risk for capital market issuance as well. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0526 ET - U.K. borrowing costs have been falling across all maturities since the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  relaxed its stance on the outlook of interest-rate rises at its March meeting, says \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  . On Monday, "gilt yields finished lower across the curve, with the 2-year down by 5.4bp, the 10-year by 7.8bp and the 30-year by 10.5bp," analysts at the Dutch bank say. The move was triggered by "a dovish turn from the Bank of England Governor Bailey who noted that the Bank had softened its guidance at its 17th March meeting owing to a looming squeeze on real household incomes that is set to exceed that seen in the 1970s." U.K. 10-year gilt yields last trade at 1.69% and two-year yields at 1.39%, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2  . (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0523 ET - S&P Global Ratings has wasted no time in rushing to affirm Australia's AAA sovereign credit rating and stable outlook following the release of the Australian federal government's budget for 2022-2023 at 0830 GMT. Australia's economic recovery is improving and the government's fiscal trajectory faster than it previously anticipated, S&P says. Federal and state governments' budget deficits will narrow toward 3% of GDP over the next two years. The budget revealed a materially lower deficit in fiscal 2022 of 3.9% of GDP compared with a forecast of 5.5% of GDP made a year ago. Australia remains in a small group of 11 sovereigns with a AAA rating from S&P. (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 29, 2022 08:26 ET (12:26 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020220329ei3t001vz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
