\par\par \b \uc2 Coordinated  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 -U.S.  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seems Unlikely -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par 09:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0704 GMT - The possibility of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. to stop the yen's depreciation seems unlikely, says Daisaku Ueno, a strategist at \uc2 Mitsubishi UFJ Morgan Stanley Securities\uc2  . That's because it is more favorable for the U.S. to have a strong dollar, which helps ease inflationary pressures. It is also difficult for the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  to raise interest rates just to stop the yen's fall because its rate increases would need to match the pace of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  's in order to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the Japanese economy isn't strong enough to bear such a radical move. (megumi.fujikawa@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0703 GMT - The Russian ruble rises to a four-week high versus the dollar on hopes for a breakthrough in peace talks between Russia and Ukraine. USD/RUB falls to as low as 92.4999. Another round of Russia-Ukraine talks are set to get underway on Tuesday in Turkey and Ukraine President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelensky\uc2  has said his country could declare neutrality to end the conflict. The ruble is supported by optimism surrounding the talks as well as mandatory sales of Russian exporters' foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenues, Unicredit Research says. "At the same time, however, investors remain prudent about new effective steps towards a diplomatic solution to the conflict." (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0701 GMT - Reaching 0.70% is within the realm of possible outcomes for the 10-year German Bund yield, mostly dragged by U.S. markets, but it isn't a done deal, say ING's rates strategists. "The main risk to our view is a deterioration in sentiment," they add. They point to geopolitics, but add that more broadly, sharp rises in rates have had a tendency to generate their own risk-off reactions. The 10-year Bund yield is trading 3 basis points higher at 0.610%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0648 GMT - South Korea's Kospi added 0.4% to close at 2741.07, supported by gains in auto, airline and tech stocks. Renewed hopes for fresh ceasefire talks between Russia and Ukraine helped buoy investor sentiment, stoking risk appetite. USD/KRW settled 0.6% lower at 1,219.80 in Seoul trade on risk-on sentiment. Auto-components maker \uc2 Mando\uc2  jumped 8.6% on hopes that its 1Q earnings could beat street views. Car maker \uc2 Hyundai Motor\uc2  gained 1.2%. Budget airline \uc2 Jin Air\uc2  rose 4.7%. Memory-chip maker \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2  added 1.7%. Meanwhile, \uc2 Korea Electric Power\uc2  lost 2.8% after a government decision against an additional tariffs increase in 2Q. \uc2 Samsung Electronics\uc2  was 0.7% higher. (kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0647 GMT - The willingness of companies in Germany to hire new staff has taken a knock, the \uc2 Ifo Institute\uc2  says. The Ifo employment barometer fell to 102.1 points in March from 104.3 points in February, falling to its lowest level since May 2021. The current high level of uncertainty in the economy due to Russia's attack on Ukraine is making companies more cautious when it comes to personnel planning, Ifo says. In manufacturing, the employment barometer fell noticeably, as companies still want to hire, but to a lesser degree, Ifo data shows. The indicator fell in the service sector too, but is still at a high level, Ifo says. However, trade and construction are currently reluctant to create new jobs, Ifo says. (maria.martinez@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0643 GMT - The FTSE 100 is expected to open higher as investors look ahead to another round of peace talks between Russia and Ukraine in Turkey aimed at ending the conflict. Spreadbetting firm IG sees London's blue-chip index rising 30 points. The Russia-Ukraine talks are expected to get underway Tuesday and Ukraine President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelensky\uc2  has said his country could declare neutrality to secure peace. "Markets are always keen to price in the prospect of a peace deal, if one could call it that, with what might be hints of concessions by both sides," Oanda says. A breakthrough would push oil prices and safe havens including the dollar and gold lower while sending the euro and European equities higher, Oanda says. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0636 GMT - There are indications that the German Bund curve is about to join the flattening trend seen in the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  curve for a year, says UniCredit Research. "Since money markets are pricing in the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's first rate hike in early September, we would regard it as reasonable if the Bund curve were now to enter a flattening trend," they add. They say that the 2-10-year segment of the Bund curve closed flatter on four of the past five trading days. The 2-10-year German yield spread is around 69 basis points, with the 10-year Bund yield trading 3.5 basis points higher at 0.615%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0621 GMT - Eurozone government-bond yields rise early Tuesday and \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  's rates strategists see current levels as an entry opportunity. "Higher yields should actually lead to higher demand, but the opposite seems to be the case," they say. However, as flows should support demand soon, they would go tactically long in 10-year German Bunds at 0.6% on Tuesday, they say. The 10-year Bund yield is trading 2.7 basis points higher at 0.606%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0618 GMT - Japanese stocks end higher, led by gains in auto and tech stocks, as concerns ease over rising costs of fuel and raw materials. \uc2 Toyota Motor\uc2  adds 2.7% and medical-information platform operator M3 gains 4.6%. The Nikkei Stock Average rises 1.1% to 28252.42. The 10-year Japanese government bond yield falls half a basis point to 0.245% as the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  conducts fixed-rate bond-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit yield gains. Investors remain focused on the war in Ukraine and its trade implications as Russia and Ukraine prepare to hold cease-fire talks in Turkey. USD/JPY is at 123.53, compared with 123.89 as of Monday 5 p.m. Eastern Time. (kosaku.narioka@wsj.com; @kosakunarioka)\par \par \uc2 0618 GMT - USD/SGD is trading steadily in the Asian afternoon session amid quarter-end and month-end flows. These flows could distort price action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, Maybank says. Besides the Russia-Ukraine war and markets pricing in prospects of a faster pace of Fed rate increases, the status of global growth will likely be a focus, Maybank says, noting this week's release of global PMIs. On the daily technical chart, USD/SGD's momentum and relative-strength-index indicators aren't showing a clear bias, Maybank adds, pegging resistance at 1.3620 and support at 1.3520. USD/SGD is little changed at 1.3606. (ronnie.harui@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0205 GMT - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen against the U.S. dollar amid mild risk appetite spurred by gains in most regional equity markets and in U.S. stock futures. The decline in crude oil prices may also provide catalysts for some positive performance during Tuesday's session, IG says, noting that China, Japan, South Korea and Taiwan are major oil importers. USD/CNY edges 0.1% lower to 6.3670, USD/KRW drops 0.2% to 1,220.89 and USD/TWD is down 0.1% at 28.79. (ronnie.harui@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0016 GMT - Japanese stocks rise, led by gains in electronics and machinery stocks, thanks to the yen's weakening and some declines in crude oil prices overnight. \uc2 Lasertec\uc2  adds 2.2% and \uc2 Komatsu\uc2  is 2.5% higher. USD/JPY is at 123.54, up from 123.23 as of Monday's Tokyo stock market close. Investors are paying attention to the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  's bond-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at limiting yield gains, as well as the war in Ukraine and its implications on commodity prices. The Nikkei Stock Average is up 0.6% at 28117.07. (kosaku.narioka@wsj.com; @kosakunarioka)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 29, 2022 03:04 ET (07:04 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020220329ei3t000oa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
