\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Japan, US to communicate closely on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  as yen hits 6-year low\b0\par\par\uc2 586 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par 10:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Japan, U.S. discussed markets particularly dollar-yen - Kanda\par \par \uc2 * Japan, U.S. underscored need to stick to G7, G20 commitments\par \par \uc2 * Kanda warns against excess volatility, disorderly \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves (Adds analyst comment, details)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 29 (Reuters) - Japan and the United States agreed to communicate closely on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues, Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat said on Tuesday in his strongest statement yet since the yen's decline to six-year lows against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Masato Kanda, vice finance minister for international affairs, also said that "excess volatility and disorderly \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves" would hurt the economy.\par \par \uc2 "We discussed financial market developments including dollar-yen moves," Kanda told reporters after meeting his counterpart Andy Baukol, acting Under Secretary of International Affairs at the \uc2 U.S. Department of the Treasury\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We underscored the importance of maintaining previous G7 and G20 commitments on exchange rates," Kanda, who oversees G7/G20 meetings and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said after the meeting at Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF).\par \par \uc2 Kanda's remarks underscore Japan's growing concern over yen declines that some lawmakers say have inflated already rising import costs for energy and food.\par \par \uc2 The visit to Tokyo by a senior U.S. official, and the two sides' rare discussion of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues, indicated Japan's and the United States' shared concern over the yen's weakening, a Japanese MOF official told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 -U.S. meeting may edge Tokyo closer to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some market players saw the yen's current levels as not weak enough to justify that.\par \par \uc2 "It's true the yen's fall has picked up pace of declines, making some people worried about excessive falls," said Masafumi Yamamoto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The tone of warning from Japanese policymakers has not much changed. MOF bureaucrats must be aware that verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be effective in reversing the (weak-yen) trend."\par \par \uc2 The prospect of aggressive U.S. interest rate hikes and the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's decisive moves to defend its 0.25% yield cap have pushed the yen to six-year lows against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The yen has lost almost 7% against the greenback so far this year. It last traded at 123.63 per dollar after falling as low as 125.10 on Monday, its lowest since August 2015.\par \par \uc2 Japanese policymakers have escalated their warnings over the impact of sharp yen falls on the world's third-biggest economy as it struggles to recover from the impact of the pandemic and as the war in Ukraine further increased the cost of oil.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Tuesday, Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  said the government will closely watch \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves to prevent a "bad" weak yen that hurts the economy.\par \par \uc2 "Based on the G7 and G20 agreements, we will closely communicate with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities from the United States and other countries to respond appropriately," Kanda said.\par \par \uc2 Kanda declined to comment when asked whether the "close communication" between \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the United States was meant to include \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Given the economy's heavy reliance on exports, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has historically focused on arresting sharp yen rises and taken a hands-off approach on yen falls.\par \par \uc2 Yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to arrest steep yen falls has been very rare, with the latest action taken during the Asian financial crisis in 1998. (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Writing by Leika Kihara; Editing by Christopher Cushing & Shri Navaratnam and Barbara Lewis) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-3-29T09:47:41.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220329ei3t008c1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
