\par\par \b \uc2 BUZZ-COMMENT-Japan shuts  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  stable door after yen horse has bolted\b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par 10:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 March 29 (Reuters) - Yen bears hope the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bond \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to speak louder than words on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Japanese government officials, as this could help inflate USD/JPY to 130, if not 135.\par \par \uc2 The BoJ kept up its quest to defend a key yield cap by offering to buy unlimited amounts of 10-year government bonds on Tuesday -- a quest that is putting downward pressure on the yen. Japanese government officials also ramped up warnings against sharp yen falls on Tuesday, a day after USD/JPY hit 125 for the first time since August 2015.\par \par \uc2 The possibility of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  moving beyond jawboning and ordering the BoJ to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to strengthen the yen would be higher were it not for the \uc2 BoJ\uc2 's "yield curve control" strategy. Unless the BoJ unexpectedly ditches YCC, scope for 50 basis point rate hikes from the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  in the second and third quarters should only widen the already cavernous 10-year UST-JGB yield spread, and support USD/JPY.\par \par \uc2 Related comments:\par \par \uc2 For more click on\par \par \uc2 (Robert Howard is a Reuters market analyst. The views expressed are his own)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-4-1T08:46:35.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220329ei3t01ejh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
