\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen on the ropes as \uc2 BOJ\uc2  defends yield target\b0\par\par\uc2 642 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par 03:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Tom Westbrook\par     SINGAPORE, March 29 (Reuters) - The yen fought for a footing\par on Tuesday, following its worst session in 16 months, as the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  pins down bond yields at a time when they are\par rising sharply in the rest of the world.\par     The Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell as much as 2.4% to\par 125.10 to the dollar overnight, its lowest since August 2015,\par before recovering to 124.24 in volatile morning trade in Tokyo.\par     The U.S. dollar was broadly steady elsewhere, keeping the\par euro at $1.0988 and capping a recent rally in the\par Australian dollar to hold it at $0.7483.\par     Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought a little more than $500 million\par in bonds on Monday and has vowed three more days of unlimited\par purchases to defend its 10-year yield target of 0.25%.\par \par     The move, a demonstration of resolve to keep Japan's\par monetary policy ultra easy, underscores the stark contrast with\par an ever-more-hawkish sounding \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  and has\par tipped the already-sliding yen off a cliff.\par     It is down nearly 7% this month and almost 10% on a\par resurgent Aussie. But with Japanese government bond\par yields (JGBs) barely retreating it is clear that\par some investors doubt the longevity of Japan's policy.\par     "Anyone who watched the \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBA\f28 \uc2 \f2  'cap' blow is probably excitedly\par (and logically) short JGBs right now hoping for a similar move\par in Japan rates," said Brent Donnelly, president at analytics\par firm Spectra Markets, referring to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of\par Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's abandonment of its yield target in November.\par     Minutes from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's March meeting published on\par Tuesday showed policymakers stressing the need to keep monetary\par policy ultra-loose, even as some of them saw signs of growing\par inflationary pressure.\par     Yet economists see building pressure for a shift if\par persistent yen weakness exacerbates inflation by raising import\par costs, particularly for energy, and reckon that 125, roughly\par where dollar/yen peaked in 2015, is a key level.\par     "Japanese yen depreciation is a big problem for the Japanese\par economy, because the economy - especially households - is facing\par rising inflation and yen depreciation could accelerate that,"\par said Kentaro Koyama, chief economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Tokyo.\par     "If the dollar/yen rate exceeded 125 I'd expect some more\par severe verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     Japanese Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shunichi Suzuki\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Tuesday\par that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will carefully watch \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market movement\par to avoid "bad yen weakening".\par     Among other majors the New Zealand dollar was a\par fraction weaker at $0.6889 and sterling was under\par pressure at $1.3081.\par     European consumer confidence data and U.S. job openings\par figures are due later in the day.\par     \par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0105 GMT\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct     High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                 \par                                               Session                                           \par  Euro/Dollar                  $1.0975        $1.0988     -0.10%         -3.45%      +1.0998     +1.0969\par  Dollar/Yen                   123.8750       123.8650    +0.20%         +7.91%      +124.3000   +123.4000\par  Euro/Yen         <EURJPY=EB  135.98         136.13      -0.11%         +4.34%      +136.5100   +135.5400\par                   S>                                                                            \par  Dollar/Swiss                 0.9342         0.9345      -0.02%         +2.43%      +0.9356     +0.9334\par  Sterling/Dollar              1.3083         1.3095      -0.10%         -3.27%      +1.3106     +1.3080\par  Dollar/Canadian              1.2522         1.2517      +0.04%         -0.96%      +1.2530     +1.2515\par  Aussie/Dollar                0.7479         0.7492      -0.16%         +2.90%      +0.7507     +0.7475\par  NZ                           0.6891         0.6897      -0.07%         +0.69%      +0.6908     +0.6889\par  Dollar/Dollar                                                                                  \par                                                                                                 \par     \par All spots\par Tokyo spots\par Europe spots \par Volatilities \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par \par     \par  (Reporting by Tom Westbrook.\par Editing by Shri Navaratnam)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-3-29T02:18:07.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220329ei3t004jx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
