\par\par \b \uc2 Global  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  and Fixed Income Roundup: Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 2021\par 08:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2021, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The latest Market Talks covering \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Fixed Income. Published exclusively on Dow Jones Newswires throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 0700 GMT - Eurozone noncore government bond yield spreads are still rather low by historical standards and they look vulnerable to a shift in the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's narrative next year, Florian Spaete, senior bond strategist at \uc2 Generali Investments\uc2  , says. "The tighter \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity will dampen the current carry-friendly low volatility environment," while an expected increase in core yields will reduce the search for yield, he says. However, solid growth, still accommodative monetary policy and the support from the NextGenerationEU program will prevent a disorderly increase in risk premiums, he says, forecasting moderate spread widening in 2022. Presidential elections in Italy and France have the potential to have a lasting impact on the current calm political environment, Spaete says, expecting it to become bumpier in 2022. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0640 GMT - China is likely to take more steps to limit the fallout for its debt-riddled property sector, but this doesn't mean it will rescue all troubled developers, \uc2 UOB\uc2  reckons. "While China's property sector, taken as a whole, is of systemic importance to the overall economy, individual property developers would not be considered systematically important," the Singapore bank says. It estimates property developers and related sectors, including heavy-equipment and building-material suppliers, have debt equivalent to 35% of China's financial system or 100% of China's GDP. Should signs of contagion grow, \uc2 UOB\uc2  expects state-owned banks will find a way to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (yongchang.chin@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0619 GMT - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Nikkei Stock Average climbed 2.1% to close at 28517.59 as U.S. stock futures rose and the yen weakened. Equities in Asia including Japan are higher, thanks to a wave of short-covering sharply lifting U.S. stock futures, Oanda says. Top performers on the Nikkei included \uc2 Lasertec\uc2 , rising 4.9%, and \uc2 Advantest\uc2 , gaining 4.6%. \uc2 Shionogi & Co\uc2  . jumped 5.3% after saying Monday that its oral drug has high antiviral activity against Covid-19's Omicron variant. Meanwhile, Kobe Bussan lost 0.9% and Daifuku shed 0.5%. USD/JPY was at 113.74, compared with 113.44 at Monday's Tokyo stock market close. The yield on the 10-year Japanese government bond was up 1.5 basis points at 0.050%. (ronnie.harui@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 21, 2021 02:01 ET (07:01 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020211221ehcl000cf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
