\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan policy veteran Kanda to be appointed as  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  tsar -sources\b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 2021\par 12:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, background)\par \par \uc2 By Takaya Yamaguchi\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 29 (Reuters) - Japan is likely to appoint international policy veteran Masato Kanda as its top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official representing the country at \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  (G7) and broader G20 meetings, four government sources with knowledge of the matter told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Currently serving as the international bureau chief at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Kanda will replace Kenji Okamura, who will retire next month after serving in his post for a year, the sources said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The sources spoke on condition of anonymity as they are not authorised to speak to media.\par \par \uc2 The appointment, which will take effect in July following a nod from Prime Minister \uc2 Yoshihide Suga\uc2 's cabinet, comes at a time when Japan is coordinating with G7/G20 to curb the COVID-19 pandemic as well as tackle global tax and emerging market debt.\par \par \uc2 Kanda, as vice finance minister for international affairs, would oversee any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary to prevent \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-led economy from slipping back into recession.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since the aftermath of the 2011 earthquake and nuclear crisis, although authorities tend to verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem spikes in the yen that risk hurting the export-reliant economy.\par \par \uc2 Kanda is known for his broad experience and close ties with policymakers at home and overseas, having worked closely with the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  as deputy vice minister for policy planning and coordination.\par \par \uc2 Kanda is also close to BOJ Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2 , who was vice finance minister for international affairs for 3-1/2 years to January 2003.\par \par \uc2 The government is set to name Koji Yano, as administrative vice finance minister - the top bureaucrat at the finance ministry - to replace Mitsuru Ota who is retiring, the sources said.\par \par \uc2 For three years from 2012, Yano worked as secretary of Suga who then was serving as government's top spokesperson. (Reporting by Takaya Yamaguchi; Writing by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Alison Williams) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-6-29T11:12:17.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210629eh6t01jmu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
