\par\par \b \uc2 Binance Crypto Exchange Ordered to Cease U.K. Activities -- 2nd Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anna Hirtenstein \par \uc2 537 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2021\par 02:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2021, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Authorities in the U.K. and Japan took aim at affiliates of Binance Holdings Ltd., the world's largest cryptocurrency exchange network, in the latest regulatory crackdown on the wildly popular trade in bitcoin and other digital assets.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.K. Financial Conduct Authority\uc2 , the country's lead financial regulator, told consumers Saturday that Binance's local unit wasn't permitted to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  related to regulated financial activities.\par \par \uc2 Binance offers trading of cryptocurrencies and derivatives linked to them such as futures. Binance Markets Ltd., the company's U.K. arm, applied to be registered with the \uc2 Financial Conduct Authority\uc2  and withdrew its application on May 17.\par \par \uc2 "A significantly high number of cryptoasset businesses are not meeting the required standards" under money-laundering regulations, said a spokesperson for the FCA in an email. "Of the firms we've assessed to date, over 90% have withdrawn applications following our \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial watchdog issued a statement on June 25, saying that Binance isn't registered to do business in the country.\par \par \uc2 The price of bitcoin whipsawed over the weekend after the regulatory moves, falling as much as 6% from its level at 5 p.m. ET on Friday before recovering all the lost ground and trading around $33,250 on Sunday, according to data from CoinDesk. In mid-April, it was above $63,000.\par \par \uc2 As of April, Binance operated the largest cryptocurrency exchange in the world by trading volume, allowing tens of billions of dollars of trades to pass through its networks, according to data provider CryptoCompare. It was founded in 2017 and initially based in China, later moving offices to Japan and Malta. It recently said it is a decentralized organization with no headquarters.\par \par \uc2 In recent months, Binance has begun offering "stock tokens," or units of digital \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that track the value of stocks such as \uc2 Tesla Inc\uc2 . and \uc2 Apple Inc\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The U.K.'s \uc2 FCA\uc2  has taken a wary stance on cryptocurrencies, earlier this year instituting a ban on individual investors trading cryptocurrency derivatives. In its statement Saturday about Binance, it warned consumers to be careful of online advertisements promising high returns on crypto investments.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FCA\uc2  move doesn't ban customers from using Binance completely. U.K. customers can continue to use Binance's non-U.K. \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  for activities the \uc2 FCA\uc2  doesn't directly regulate, such as buying and selling direct holdings in bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 "The FCA U.K. notice has no direct impact on the services provided on Binance.com. Our relationship with our users has not changed," said a Binance spokesperson by email.\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrencies have come under fire for their use in illegal activities such as money laundering, ransoms and fraud. The digital \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are often unregulated, but derivatives linked to them are generally overseen by national regulators including the U.K.'s \uc2 FCA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 China also has recently intensified its crackdown on cryptocurrencies. Its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said last week that the country's largest banks and payment processors should take an active role in curbing cryptocurrency trading and related activities.