\par\par \b \uc2 BUZZ-U.S.  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Markets Open - December 24\b0\par\par\uc2 903 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 2020\par 12:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Pound rises ahead of expected Brexit trade deal Market Briefs \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD 0.08%, USD/JPY 0.08%, GBP/USD 0.8%, EUR/GBP -0.68% \u8226\'20\'22 DXY -0.24%, DAX 1.26%, FTSE -0.18%, Brent -0.57%, Gold 0.15% \u8226\'20\'22 On cusp of Brexit trade deal, EU and UK haggle over fish \u8226\'20\'22 Sterling awaits Brexit deal confirmation, approaches 2-1/2-year high \u8226\'20\'22 Democrats want rushed vote on Trump's $2,000 coronavirus aid checks \u8226\'20\'22 Turkish cenbank hikes 200 bps to 17% in credibility test \u8226\'20\'22 BOJ's Kuroda to seek ways to make stimulus 'nimble' in review \u8226\'20\'22 Saudi oil exports in October fall by almost a third Looking Ahead - Economic Data (GMT) \u8226\'20\'22 13:30 CA Nov Building Permits MM, 3% f'cast, -14.6% prev Looking Ahead - Events, Other Releases (GMT) \u8226\'20\'22 No major event scheduled Commentary and Analysis EUR/USD more likely to gain than fall as dollar remains soft \u8226\'20\'22 GBP gains, USD on back foot amid hopes Brexit deal imminent \u8226\'20\'22 Large long lower shadow on Mon's candle line props up EUR/USD \u8226\'20\'22 Positive alignment of the tenkan and kijun lines \par \par \uc2 highlight the bullish bias \u8226\'20\'22 Setbacks on Tuesday and Wednesday have failed to drop under Mon's 1.2130 low \u8226\'20\'22 Thursday has seen a tight EUR/USD 1.2185-1.2216 EBS range so far \u8226\'20\'22 Euro demand could grow in the New Year \u8226\'20\'22 Recent EUR/USD longs offload great news for bulls USD/JPY upside limited, Watanabe gives view on 100 defence \u8226\'20\'22 Watanabe: \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to arrest yen rise but only once \u8226\'20\'22 Former \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat skeptical authorities could keep USD/JPY above 100 \u8226\'20\'22 Sell-rally strategies seems to dominate USD/JPY, limiting its upside \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY has seen a tight 103.50-69 EBS range so far on Christmas eve \u8226\'20\'22 Long upper shadow on Monday's candle continues to weigh heavily on USD/JPY \u8226\'20\'22 \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders should seek downside insurance into 2021 \u8226\'20\'22 Kuroda: BOJ ready to make stimulus more sustainable GBP/USD up to eye 31-month high on Brexit deal expectation \u8226\'20\'22 Cable hits 1.3617 as GBP continues to benefit from expected EU-UK trade deal \u8226\'20\'22 1.3617 is eight pips shy of last week's 31-month high \u8226\'20\'22 1.3617 is four-and-a-quarter cents above Monday's 10-day low (1.3190) \u8226\'20\'22 GBP/EUR has simultaneously risen to 1.1166, its highest level since Dec 1 \u8226\'20\'22 1.1166 is over three cents above Monday's 10-day low \u8226\'20\'22 1.3569 (Wednesday's high) is now a GBP/USD support point. 1.3562 = Asia high AUD/USD helped to three-day high by expected Brexit deal \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/USD up to 0.7603 as risk-sensitive AUD benefits from expected EU-UK deal \u8226\'20\'22 0.7603 = three-day high: 0.7606 was Monday's high \u8226\'20\'22 0.7639 (last week's 30-month high) is a resistance level beyond 0.7606 \u8226\'20\'22 Recent AUD gains have been influenced by higher commodity prices \u8226\'20\'22 China iron ore futures bounce back after two days of falls \u8226\'20\'22 Copper near eight-year high. A$342mn 0.7600 expiry for NY cut USD/JPY chart likely to defeat Japan authorities Japan's defense of 100.00 yen to the dollar, the near- and long-term bearish charts and the recent reduction of speculative shorts all point to a steeper USD/JPY decline in the weeks ahead. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the yen from strengthening past 100 to the dollar, but just once given the difficulty of keeping \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates pegged at a set level, former top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Hiroshi Watanabe said on Thursday. A USD/JPY close at the end of December below the 200-month moving average, now at 103.90, would weaken the structure of the long-term USD/JPY chart. That would increase the odds for a steeper drop to test the March 101.18 low, then the under-100.00 level that Japan's PM Suga shined a bright light on. Once USD/JPY is under 100.00, that would expose the 2016 99.000 low and longer-term the major 94.621 Fibonacci level, a 61.8% retrace of the 75.311 to 125.86 (2011 to 2015) EBS rise. Pound will be fishing in uncharted waters in 2021 Having spent so long at the whim of \uc2 European Union\uc2 -UK negotiations, sterling will find itself in the unusual position of looking elsewhere for market-moving influences in 2021. Those influences will include Britain's ability to get to grips with the COVID-19 pandemic and the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2 's monetary policy -- which will be closely intertwined. The pound could benefit if the BoE is unexpectedly hawkish: on Wednesday, BoE chief economist \uc2 Andy Haldane\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must have a laser focus on keeping inflation expectations in check once the COVID-19 crisis eases. GBP/USD rose to threaten last week's 31-month high of 1.3625 on Thursday, with GBP/EUR rising to its highest level since Dec. 1, 1.1168, ahead of the expected announcement of an EU-UK trade deal. CFTC data for the week to Dec. 22, due on Monday (Dec. 28), will show if the net GBP long position held by IMM speculators grew or shrank as Brexit negotiations entered the final strait.\par \par \uc2 To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-12-27T11:54:59.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201224egco01b59\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
