\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Discovers the Problem With Yield-Curve Control -- It Works Too Well -- Barrons.com\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steve Goldstein \par \uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2020\par 14:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2020, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Albert Edwards\uc2 , the veteran \uc2 Soci\u233\'00\'E9t\u233\'00\'E9 G\u233\'00\'E9n\u233\'00\'E9rale\uc2  strategist who is famously bearish, has long looked to Japan to tell the deflationary story he foresees for the rest of the industrialized world.\par \par \uc2 One policy being considered by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  that is already implemented by the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  is yield curve control. Federal Reserve Chairman \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interest-rate setting committee was briefed on the policy during the June meeting.\par \par \uc2 The simple version of that policy is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  commits not to let bond yields exceed a certain level.\par \par \uc2 A recent \uc2 New York Fed\uc2  paper concluded that the policy does have a strong impact -- the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't had to resort to large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Japanese government bond market. While the \uc2 New York Fed\uc2  views that as a success, Edwards sees that impact as a flaw.\par \par \uc2 Less bond buying means less \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation, he says.\par \par \uc2 Maybe the point of quantitative easing is "actually to drive down your own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as occurred in Japan with dramatic effect at the end of 2012 when [Prime Minister Shinzo] Abe took office with a commitment to take a more aggressive monetary policy stance. Indeed, I have always been of the opinion that this is the only effective transmission mechanism for QE to stimulate an economy -- and indeed despite their denials that is certainly the route that the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gone down in copying Japan's weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," he says.\par \par \uc2 Comments coming from the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , he says, suggest the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has realized the error of its way. He notes headlines coming out saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to closely cooperate with the fiscal side, given increased government bond issuance.\par \par \uc2 "And this is exactly what the Ice Age endgame always was. 'Cooperation' here is a euphemism for full blown monetization of the government deficit. The endgame is in sight as we transition to The Great Melt. The veil is finally being lifted and once again, Japan leads the way," says Edwards.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 24, 2020 08:25 ET (12:25 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020200624eg6o001ff\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 Positive start to huge week\b0\par\par\uc2 CMC Markets \par \uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2020\par 01:58\par \uc2 Fuseworks Media\par \uc2 FUSMED\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020. Fuseworks Limited. \par \par \uc2 By Michael McCarthy (chief market strategist, CMC Markets and Stockbroking)\par \par \uc2 Asia Pacific markets are set for a growth positive start to trading after a rally in US shares and modest pressure on safe haven assets on Friday night. However a the market calendar suggests some caution ahead of interest rate decisions from major central banks, inflation, GDP and other economic data from leading nations, and the busiest week of the US company reporting season.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are range bound ahead of meetings of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2  and the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 . The lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement reflects expectations that all three will maintain current settings after the massive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  introduced at out-of-cycle emergency meetings.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Australia, Italy, Germany, the US and France all release inflation data this week, in that order. Hong Kong and New Zealand trade numbers, Singapore industrial production, China PMIs, and Japanese retail sales provide regional highlights against a backdrop of European GDP reads and US flash national accounts. A larger than expected 14.4% drop in US durable goods orders on Friday night sounds a warning that investors are potentially facing hard evidence of virus related macro-economic damage.\par \par \uc2 The action starts today with Hong Kong trade numbers and the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's meeting and policy decision.\par \par \uc2 Around 170 SPX 500 companies will report to shareholders this week. The first quarter contains less than one month of virus affected trading, but reports so far show a collective hit of around 18% to bottom lines. Investor reactions to further bad news are a key to the likely market outcomes. Tech giants are the main driver of index gains over the last three years, meaning Thursday's reports from \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and Apple will receive particular attention.\par \par \uc2 Dokument FUSMED0020200427eg4q00001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
