\par\par \b \uc2 Japanese Yen to Outperform Swiss Franc as Safe Haven: \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2020\par 17:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2020, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1115 ET - The Japanese yen should outperform the Swiss franc on any escalation in geopolitical concerns, \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  says. The yen and the franc, which are considered safe haven assets, are the best-performing G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since last Thursday as U.S. -Iran tensions grow, \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  's \uc2 Jane Foley\uc2  says. Persistent gains in these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  "will not be welcomed by the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  or the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  ," she says. The policies of the two central banks are "positioned to reduce the appeal" of speculative inflows into their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but Switzerland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  goes "one step further" than \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  by threatening \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That means the outlook for JPY/CHF would be "moderately higher" on increased geopolitical worries. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1111 ET - The U.K. economy is likely to take a hit from its "ill-advised" plan to leave the EU , says \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  . The investment bank expects the country's GDP to rise by an average of 1.3% this year, but to fade thereafter. Investment strategist Sebastian Raedler says the U.K. is removing itself from the most advantageous trading arrangement it could have with the EU by leaving the bloc. "Withdrawing from a mutually beneficial arrangement is ill-advised," he says. "GDP might be lower by 6-7% in the long run because you're choosing a sub-optimal model." (philip.waller@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1110 ET - Spain's long road to forming a government could come to a provisional conclusion in Tuesday's parliamentary ballot, but still the future of the socialist PSOE and left-wing UP alliance is uncertain without its own majority, leaving Spain politically unstable, says \uc2 DZ Bank\uc2  . The ERC party, which aspires to Catalonia's independence, will have to abstain from the vote to enable a simple majority in the upcoming, second vote. The end of the political vacuum and the less rigid attitude of coalition members toward Catalonia would be positive from a market perspective, but the risk of early failure of the coalition remains high in view of the limited room for manoeuver, he says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1104 ET - The euro is likely to remain stuck in a $1.110-$1.1250 range for the time being as the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kicks off a review of its monetary policy strategy, \uc2 BMO Capital Markets\uc2  says. The \uc2 ECB\uc2  's inflation target is one of the key areas of its strategic review starting January, meaning investors "should look through upside misses" on core consumer price inflation data, BMO \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist \uc2 Stephen Gallo\uc2  says. "Though alterations to the \uc2 ECB\uc2  's reaction function could further inflame intra-euro political tensions, we can't help but think that [Fabio] Schnabel's appointment to the executive board will initially push the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the direction of tolerating higher rates of inflation for longer." EUR/USD rises 0.3% to 1.1188.(renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1103 ET - The Turkish lira is likely to fall further against the dollar in coming months as risk appetite weakens on escalating U.S.-Iran tensions, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says. The U.S. killing of Iranian general \uc2 Qassem Soleimani\uc2  Friday, provides "little reassurance that a risk-off scenario can be excluded in the near-term," \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  analysts say in a note. An acceleration in Turkish inflation in December also "does not bode well for the lira" while monetary policy measures by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are "not having any effect whatsoever" on curbing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's depreciation. USD/TRY is last flat on the day at 5.9725. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1048 ET - Debt investors should not pin expectations for tightening credit spreads exclusively on corporate bond purchases by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as its effect "seems to be waning," say ABN AMRO 's fixed-income strategists. "While we expect an upscale in the level of purchases from April onwards, we would not bank on spread tightening purely from this event," they say. "We get a feeling that the technical support no longer has meaningful impact on spreads as it did when it [the corporate bond purchases program] was first announced back in early 2016." While \uc2 ECB\uc2  's bond purchases may have lost their power pushing spreads lower, a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  presence "does keep spreads anchored," they say.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 1004 ET - Securities written to provide insurance on the \uc2 US government\uc2  's creditworthiness may be sending a misleading message, \uc2 New York Fed\uc2  research says. Starting in 2014, the volume of activity essentially dropped out of the quotes for US credit-default swaps, the analysis says. "Quoted CDS spreads in this market are based on few, if any, transactions," the research says. "Are the quoted US sovereign CDS spreads a useful measure of market participants' expectations of US sovereign credit risk? ... This is unlikely to be the case," the bank adds. The paper's finding is useful because it suggests the next time US CDS moves around some budget brinkmanship, it may not be sending a real read on what markets think about the risks around government borrowing and debt service. (michael.derby@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0947 ET - Despite a mixed macro picture and tensions in the Middle East, euro-denominated corporate debt issuance is poised "to start with a bang" in January after the lull Christmas period, says \uc2 ABN AMRO\uc2  . "European firms have been facing a significant funding gap, which had not been made up by new net issuance in the 2019," says the bank. This, coupled with central banks' easing monetary policies keeping "funding conditions at decent levels," is likely to unleash more new bond sales, it says.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0932 ET - The WSJ Dollar Index declined 0.2% to a recent 89.78, pushed lower versus \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  supported by the recent rise in oil prices including the Canadian dollar and the Norwegian krone. The dollar also weakened against the euro after a purchasing manager survey data showed the region's service was stronger last month than initial estimates had shown. Data also showed that German retail sales rose 2.1% in November from the month before, which was more than twice the gain expected by some economists. (daniel.kruger@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0917 ET - \uc2 US government\uc2  bond prices rise amid concerns about escalating tensions between the US and Iran. Yields on US Treasurys have fallen so far this year after a US strike killed a leading Iranian general following a number of attacks on Iraqi bases where US troops were stationed. The decline has reversed a recent rise in yields to near their highest in months as investors had pared holdings of safe government debt in favor of stocks, which had climbed to record highs. The yield on the benchmark 10-year Treasury note was a recent 1.783% compared with 1.787% Friday. (daniel.kruger@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0829 ET - The euro will struggle to rise considerably against the dollar unless Germany raises fiscal spending to lift the economy out of the doldrums, \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  says. "The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has done almost everything that it can to revive growth, and yet we still see Germany slipping into recession in 2020," \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  analysts say. "Maybe loosening the fiscal purse strings requires progress on banking union or even fiscal union." Without easier fiscal policy, the euro "cannot really rally that far." \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  expects EUR/USD to rise to 1.20 by the fourth quarter of 2020 from 1.1203 currently with the euro "helped by the simple fact that it is undervalued against the dollar." (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0829 ET - The recent bond outperformance of base metal issuers \uc2 Arcelor Mittal\uc2  and \uc2 Glencore\uc2  could remain volatile going forward as the U.S.-China's phase one trade deal "will not drive a V-shaped recovery", says ABN AMRO . The Dutch bank notes that tariffs between the countries remain in place and that the redirection of supply chains could harm productivity. In addition, ABN AMRO 's fixed-income strategists say stimulus entertained by China "will remain piecemeal driven." \uc2 Glencore\uc2  's 1.875% EUR June 2023 bonds have tightened to 76.538 basis points in asset swap spread terms from 91.646 bps in early December, before the deal was announced, according to Tradeweb.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 06, 2020 11:15 ET (16:15 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020200106eg160021e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
