\par\par \b \uc2 Japanese Yen to Outperform Swiss Franc as Safe Haven: \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 150 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2020\par 17:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2020, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1615 GMT - The Japanese yen should outperform the Swiss franc on any escalation in geopolitical concerns, \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  says. The yen and the franc, which are considered safe haven assets, are the best-performing G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since last Thursday as U.S. -Iran tensions grow, \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 's \uc2 Jane Foley\uc2  says. Persistent gains in these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  "will not be welcomed by the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  or the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 ," she says. The policies of the two central banks are "positioned to reduce the appeal" of speculative inflows into their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but Switzerland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  goes "one step further" than \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  by threatening \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That means the outlook for JPY/CHF would be "moderately higher" on increased geopolitical worries. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 06, 2020 11:15 ET (16:15 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020200106eg16001zj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
