\par\par \b \uc2 EUR/USD Fall Below 1.10 May Increase Talk of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 : Standard Chartered -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2019\par 12:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2019, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1039 GMT - EUR/USD's recent fall below 1.10 raises the chances of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by U.S. authorities to stem dollar strength, says \uc2 Standard Chartered Bank\uc2  , based on historic comparisons with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit rises in the Japanese yen. Modeling four \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2010-2011 and applying the formula to the current situation with EUR/USD, \uc2 Standard Chartered\uc2  concludes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  signals have "ramped up sharply over the last week." EUR/USD's sudden drop below 1.10 was probably the trigger, it says. EUR/USD dropped below 1.10 late Friday, reaching a two-year low of 1.0926 on Tuesday, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 . It has since recovered and is last up 0.1% at 1.1049. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0956 GMT - The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should acknowledge that monetary policy is exhausted and gear further measures toward supporting fiscal policy, says Andrew Bosomworth, head of portfolio management in Germany at Pimco. He finds that a policy directing at continuing to lower rates further may generate more costs than benefits, and therefore he advises against further rate cuts by the \uc2 ECB\uc2  . "Rather, the \uc2 ECB\uc2  should make clear to fiscal authorities that monetary policy is exhausted, that to boost aggregate demand they now need to increase public spending while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can remain supportive of that through a modest asset purchase program of government bonds," he says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0927 GMT - \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  changes its expectations regarding the size of an anticipated quantitative easing by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  . It now expects the \uc2 ECB\uc2  to announce at the Sept. 12 meeting the restart of QE at a monthly pace of EUR30 billion for 9-12 months, versus its previous expectation of monthly EUR45 billion for at least a year, says economist \uc2 Daniele Antonucci\uc2  . "While we think that the idea of coming up with a package still is in play, several speeches suggest that agreeing on QE is proving difficult, let alone on a relatively large one," he says, also flagging the risk that the announcement on QE is delayed. \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  also expects a 10 bps cut to the deposit rate to -0.50% together with a mechanism to mitigate the impact of negative rates. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0923 GMT - Limited risk appetite given uncertainty over this week's Brexit news headlines could weigh on Thursday's GBP2.75 billion tap of 0.875% October 2029 conventional gilts, says \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  . On a cross-market basis, the bank says gilts have underperformed versus both their equivalent U.S and \uc2 German government\uc2  bonds in the last two sessions on the back of lowering risk of no-deal Brexit, making gilts look particularly cheap historically. This means the bond offers some value compared with other government debt, and in particular relative to the U.S. 10-year Treasury, RBCCM adds. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0852 GMT - London stocks drop after the pound rises as fears about a U.K. no-deal exit from the EU recede. The FTSE 100 Index falls 0.3%, or 24.39 points to 7287.87 after the government lost a vote to hold a general election and the Commons backed a bill to prevent the country crashing out of the EU without a deal, allowing it to progress to the Lords. Sterling rises 0.2% to $1.2272. \uc2 Melrose Industries\uc2  is the top riser, up 6.1% after the industrial-turnaround specialist improved margins and said cost-cutting was protecting its automotive arm against an industry downturn. (philip.waller@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0849 GMT - The decision by the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  to leave its repo rate on hold at -0.25% this morning was never really in doubt, but its reticence to slash its forecasts for the economy leaves it well behind the curve, says David Oxley at \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  . The downward revision to the rate path is a step in the right direction, but it is still forecasting one hike towards the end of the year or at the beginning of next year, which is at odds with the weakness of domestic activity and leaves the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  well out of sync with other major central banks, he says. "In contrast, we think that the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  will have to cut interest rates, probably in December, and the market has also moved to price in looser policy in recent weeks." The Swedish krona rises after the decision, with EUR/SEK last down 0.6% at 10.6793. (dominic.chopping@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0847 GMT - EUR/USD, currently trading at 1.1040, could rise above 1.1050/1.1100 should upcoming U.S. labor data fall below expectations, although eurozone economic concerns will limit any rise, says ING. The U.S. ADP National Employment report, due 1215 GMT on Thursday, is expected to show a decline in private sector jobs created to 140,000 in August, against 156,000 jobs in July. Friday's non-farm payrolls, due 1230 GMT on Friday, is then projected to decline to 150,000 jobs created in August, from 164,000 in July, according to a WSJ poll. The euro will be held back, however, by the economic slowdown in the eurozone and the prospect of monetary easing by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sep. 12. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0831 GMT - Tanzania's gold exports are on the rise thanks to higher production and improved global prices, says the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Tanzania\uc2  . Gold shipments in the year ending July 2019 jumped 23% to hit $1.78 billion, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data shows. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes that global prices have improved, aided by high gold demand driven by US-Iran tensions, "which drove investors towards holding gold as an alternative investment." Tanzania, Africa's No.4 gold producer expects the performance of it's mining sector to rebound following a crackdown on mineral tax payments as well as the revision of it's mining law, in 2017. (Nicholas.Bariyo@wsj.com;@Nicholasbariyo)\par \par \uc2 0816 GMT - Sterling rebound is likely to be short-lived as the risks of a snap election and the possibility of a no-deal Brexit remain, says ING. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will "soon re-start a weakening trend given the election uncertainty and non-negligible risk of a no-deal Brexit should the Conservative party under Prime Minister [Boris] Johnson win a Parliamentary majority," says the bank. The pattern would mirror the price action in sterling earlier in the year, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened first on the hopes of the U.K. extending article 50 but "eventually depreciated meaningfully" as politics became more fragmented and the risk of a no-deal Brexit rose. GBP/USD is last flat at 1.2255, having jumped overnight after dropping below 1.20 on Wednesday. EUR/GBP is flat at 0.9020. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0804 GMT - The Swedish krona rises to its strongest in two weeks against the euro after the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  kept its repo rate unchanged at -0.25% and stuck to its view that the rate would rise toward the end of the year or the beginning of next year. Many in the market had expected the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  to push the rate rise forecast further out. However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still tweaked its rate forecasts lower and said the interest rate would increase at a slower pace than previously thought. EUR/SEK falls to around 10.6742, from 10.7428 just before the decision. It last trades down 0.6% at 10.6813. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0736 GMT - Sterling comes off its highs after rising sharply overnight following the U.K. parliament's approval late Wednesday of a bill aimed at blocking no-deal Brexit, as well as its rejection--for now--of snap elections. GBP/USD is last down 0.2% at 1.2230, having jumped to 1.2258 after the vote, a massive rise after it traded below 1.20 earlier in the day. EUR/GBP is last up 0.2% at 0.9024, having reached a low of 0.9000 after the vote. Uncertainty over the course of Brexit remains, however, as a snap general election before the October 31 exit deadline is still possible, says \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  . Opposition leader \uc2 Jeremy Corbyn\uc2  is likely to support a general election after the bill becomes law, it says.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0724 GMT - \uc2 Sweden's Riksbank\uc2  is expected to lower its rate path when it announces a rate decision at 0730 GMT, which is likely to cause the Swedish krona to turn lower, \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  says. Ahead of the decision the krona edges slightly higher, with EUR/SEK down 0.1% at 10.7278. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to delay the current plan to raise rates around the end of the year by one or possibly two quarters, \uc2 Danske\uc2  says. With the market already pricing in 17 basis points of rate cuts through April, this would not "come as a big surprise" but still EUR/SEK is likely to rise and test the 10.80 area, it says. "We find it hard to believe that giving up on planned rate hikes will be received as a hawkish move." (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 05, 2019 06:39 ET (10:39 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020190905ef950016c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
