\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Fear of  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  war boosts demand for shelter assets\b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 As tension between the U.S. and China influences exchange markets, policy-defining authorities in Switzerland and Japan are increasingly under pressure.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Treasury\uc2 's decision this week to label China as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator, after its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken beyond 7 yuan against the dollar, caused the values of assets considered to be safe to touch new Maximum.\par \par \uc2 Gold, which tends to rise as concern for global growth increases, has risen 14% since the beginning of the year.\par \par \uc2 The shelter coins are advancing. The yen this year is the highest-performing major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , up nearly 3% against the dollar, which traded at just 105.90 yen earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc is at its strongest against the euro since 2017, which sank at 1,0862 francs on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Both the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  (SDB) and the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  have a history of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise.\par \par \uc2 Paul Hui, exchange rate strategist at \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 , said the upsurge in the trade war will "reaffirm, expand and intensify the dominant global macro dynamic in exchange markets." This would lead to greater \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength such as yen and franc.\par \par \uc2 According to Adriel Jost, director of economics at Zurich-based wellershoff & Partners consultancy, China's decision to allow the yuan to weaken created uncertainty about the outlook for the global economy, which in turn led to strong franc demand "and is likely to lead to further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BNS."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data suggest that, in the last two weeks, the BNS began selling francs to cap the appreciation for the first time in two years.\par \par \uc2 Escalation in the trade war, coupled with the increased concern for global growth, suggests that interest in the franc and yen is likely to continue. But, amid attention around "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation" and the threat of trade wars, policy-setting authorities face tough alternatives.\par \par \uc2 They can act to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , cutting rates or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in markets, or allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen and risk damaging the local economy.\par \par \uc2 "Japan is in a world of suffering, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed on the sidelines all year and barely recycled language from last year as if nothing had changed," said Ed Al-Hussainy, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Columbia Threadneedle.\par \par \uc2 Japan's authorities, once ahead of innovative monetary policy measures, such as quantitative easing, remain cautious.\par \par \uc2 Like other central banks, the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  does not act. On Monday the dollar hit the level of 105 yen, leaving traders wondering if the entity will consider an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, the last time it did so in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was in 2011, as part of a coordinated effort with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the United States.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss authorities, for their part, are likely to continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, rather than lowering the country's key rate and placing it in negative territory.\par \par \uc2 An imponderable is the possibility of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the dollar, if trade war turns into a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war between North America and China.\par \par \uc2 As analysts expect the yuan to weaken further towards 7.5 yuan against the dollar next year, the chances of that happening increase, asJpmorgan.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190808ef8700126\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
