\par\par \b \uc2 *Japan's Top  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Official: Will Closely Watch Moves in  \highlight22\uc2 Foreign-Exchange \highlight\uc2  Rates\b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2019\par 07:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2019, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 5 Aug 2019 01:16 ET *Japan's Top \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Official: Excessive Yen Moves Aren't Desirable for Economy\par \par \uc2 5 Aug 2019 01:16 ET *Japan's Top \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Official: Will Act Against Excessive Moves in Yen if Necessary\par \par \uc2 5 Aug 2019 01:16 ET *Japan's Top \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Official: Recent Yen Moves Reflect Concerns Over US-China Trade Dispute, US Monetary Policy\par \par \uc2 5 Aug 2019 01:17 ET *Japan's Top \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Official: No Comment on Possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 5 Aug 2019 02:04 ET  \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Ready to Act Against Excessive Yen Moves -Top \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Official\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Megumi Fujikawa \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan stands ready to act against excessive moves in the yen, the country's top \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said Monday, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier rose to its strongest level in seven months against the U.S. dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Excessive moves in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates aren't desirable for the economy and finance," said Yoshiki Takeuchi, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He made the comments to reporters after meeting with Bank of Japan and Financial Services Agency officials to discuss recent developments in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We will keep in close communication with other countries," Mr. Takeuchi said. "We will make a comprehensive judgement and take appropriate action if we judge [the yen's excessive appreciation] is likely to have negative impact on our economy and finance."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Takeuchi said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , BOJ and FSA convened the urgent meeting due to the nervousness observed in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, reflecting concerns over U.S.-China trade dispute and uncertainty surrounding the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's monetary policy going forward.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The three parties had met on Aug. 1 before President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  tweeted that new, 10% tariffs would be applied on an additional $300 billion of Chinese goods starting Sept. 1.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Monday, the dollar fell below 106 yen for the first time since January. Mr. Takeuchi declined to comment on the possibility of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/JPY was last at 105.92.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Megumi Fujikawa at megumi.fujikawa@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 05, 2019 02:04 ET (06:04 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020190805ef8500092\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
