\par\par \b \uc2 Japan to name Yoshiki Takeuchi as top  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  diplomat - sources\b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2019\par 09:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 17 (Reuters) - Japan's government is set to tap Yoshiki Takeuchi as vice finance minister for international affairs, its top \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat whose duties would include arranging any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sources with knowledge of the matter told Reuters on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Takeuchi, currently international bureau chief at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , will take over from \uc2 Masatsugu Asakawa\uc2 , as part of a routine mid-year personnel reshuffle, early in July.\par \par \uc2 Takeuchi's appointment comes at a delicate time when Tokyo is under pressure from Washington to include a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  provision against \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation in the bilateral trade talks aimed at fixing what the United States says is an unfair trade balance.\par \par \uc2 Japan is resisting the inclusion of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  provision, which may tie its hands on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and monetary policies to respond to unwelcome rises in the yen that could undermine its export-reliant economy.\par \par \uc2 Asakawa, who assumed the post of the top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official in 2015, has represented Japan at meetings of the \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  advanced countries and the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  major economies.\par \par \uc2 Asakawa, who was appointed to the post in 2015, has become the longest serving top financial diplomat, exceeding the previous record set by BOJ Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2 , who served as vice finance minister for international affairs for 3-1/2 years to January 2003.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since the aftermath of the 2011 earthquake and nuclear crisis, ministry records show, though authorities tend to verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem spikes in the yen that risk hurting the export-reliant economy.\par \par \uc2 The government is set to retain Shigeaki Okamoto as administrative vice minister - the top bureaucrat at the finance ministry, the sources said on condition of anonymity because they are not authorised to speak to media. (Reporting by Takaya Yamaguch; Writing by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Jacqueline Wong) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-6-17T08:00:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190617ef6h00tef\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
