\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Could  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  If Yen Rises Further: BNY Mellon -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,508 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2019\par 15:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2019, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0917 ET - With the Japanese yen suddenly jumping to a nine-month high versus the U.S. dollar overnight on Thursday, implied volatility went up in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Were the yen to rise even further, the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, says \uc2 Neil Mellor\uc2  , senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNY Mellon. "In view of the uncertainty surrounding the health of the Japanese economy, yen strength is hardly consistent with the Bank's mandates. It is therefore perfectly possible that the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  - guided by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  - could consider returning to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Mr. Mellor says. The dollar is last down by 1% at JPY107.75, having fallen to a nine-month low of 104.79. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0904 ET - The dollar is slightly lower after mixed U.S. economic data, with EUR/USD up 0.2% at 1.1361. The ADP report showed that 271,000 jobs were added during December in the private sector, more than the 178,000 projected by a WSJ poll and the 179,000 in November. But there were also 231,000 jobless claims in December, compared with 216,000 in the previous month and more than the 220,000 claims forecast in a WSJ poll. The dollar rose slightly after the ADP report, but then reversed gains and fell before and after the jobless claims report. EUR/USD had traded around 1.1348 before the ADP data. Data from ADP could serve as guidance for Friday's non-farm payrolls, which gives a more overall picture of U.S. employment. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0853 ET - Various \uc2 European Commission\uc2  proposals and an agreement reached between the U.K. and the U.S. late last year are credit positive for U.K.-based airlines, and to a lesser extent to European Airlines, because they will limit no-fly risk in the event of a no-deal Brexit in March 2019, says Jeanine Arnold, senior credit officer at \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Investors Service. U.K.-based airlines including \uc2 British Airways\uc2  --owned by \uc2 International Consolidated Airlines Group\uc2  --, \uc2 easyJet plc\uc2  and European airlines \uc2 Wizz Air Holdings\uc2  , \uc2 Ryanair\uc2  , \uc2 Thomas Cook Group\uc2  and \uc2 Tui AG\uc2  are set to benefit the most as a significant portion of their earnings depend on EU flyover rights and/or direct flights made between the U.K. and the EU , he says. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0803 ET - The Brazilian real extended its surge against the greenback amid increasing confidence that President Bolsonaro is serious about market-friendly reform, says Pablo Spyer, from Mirae asset-management. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trading at 3.78 per dollar, stronger than 3.80 yesterday, when it was already advancing after the inauguration earlier this week. Spyer says the first speech by Economy Minister \uc2 Paulo Guedes\uc2  yesterday "corroborated market expectations" or aggressive reform. "The economy has already made an U-turn and is en route to recoup its investment grade," he said. (paulo.trevisani@wsj.com; @ptrevisani)\par \par \uc2 0752 ET - Turkey's lira has retraced much of the ground lost in the overnight flash crash but remains under pressure. It trades 1.6% lower against the dollar and 2.6% lower against the yen--despite data showing that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to ramp up interest rates have brought inflation under control following last year's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. Consumer prices rose 20.3% in December from a year before, still a rapid rate of growth, but marking the second consecutive month in which inflation has fallen. Timothy Ash, economist at \uc2 BlueBay Asset Management\uc2 , tweets that investors are concerned the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cut rates ahead of local elections on March 31, showing that past "policy failings" have saddled the bank with a "credibility gap." (joe.wallace@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0714 ET - The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  's monetary policy is likely to be data-dependent, so the ISM manufacturing index and the ADP private payrolls are likely to be key for the dollar, says \uc2 MUFG\uc2 . "The impact of surprises in the ISM report has diminished...but for surprises in the range of 2-5% the dollar response has remained strong," \uc2 MUFG\uc2  analysts say, adding "this is particularly true for negative surprises." The ADP jobs report has "typically served as a reliable preview" for the employment change data in the nonfarm payrolls report, due Friday. According to a WSJ survey, December ADP is likely to show growth of 178,000 jobs at 1315 GMT, and ISM manufacturing \uc2 PMI\uc2  is likely to come in at 57.9 at 1500 GMT. EUR/USD is flat at 1.1345. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0647 ET - The yen has potential to strengthen, say \uc2 MUFG\uc2  analysts, given that signs are building of a slowdown in global growth. The sharp overnight falls in USD/JPY to a nine-month low of 104.79, and in AUD/JPY to a nine-and-a-half-year low of 71.47, were "clearly exaggerated by the flash crash, but do reflect building fears over slowing global growth, particularly in China and Australia," the analysts say. \uc2 Apple\uc2  attributed its revenue warning to the magnitude of the economic slowdown in China, which it didn't foresee. "The developments are favorable for a stronger yen, even if the move overnight has been exaggerated," the analysts say. USD/JPY is last down by 1.2% at 107.56. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0617 ET - \uc2 Ryanair\uc2  's bond prices fall, pushing borrowing costs higher, after the Irish airline posted a 9% increase in the number of passengers carried in December to 10 million, which increased to 10.3 million after adding figures from \uc2 Laudamotion\uc2  , an Austrian low-cost subsidiary. Total passenger numbers for the 12 months through December rose 8% to 139.2 million, \uc2 Ryanair\uc2  said Thursday. This represents the lowest passenger growth in the last three years, as the budget carrier struggled with several crew strikes and bad whether among other headwinds. Bid yields on \uc2 Ryanair\uc2  's 1.125% March 2023 EUR bonds rise as high as 1.378% after the announcement from 1.334% beforehand, according to Tradeweb.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0526 ET - Debt investors's reading on Next's post-Christmas trading update released Thursday is far less enthusiastic than that of equity investors. Next's online sales rose by 15.2% but high street sales fell by 9.2% during the Christmas period, reviving recent investor worries over the ailing state the of the U.K.'s retail sector. The high street retailer's bond prices fall slightly after the announcement, pushing Next's borrowing costs up, while Next shares are up almost 3%. "Numbers from the high street stores look pretty dire, and tellingly Next expects sliding sales to continue for the next year," says \uc2 Laith Khalaf\uc2  , senior analyst at \uc2 Hargreaves Lansdown\uc2 . Bid yields on Next's 5.375% October 2021 sterling-denominated bond rise to 2.264% after the company's announcement, from 2.222% beforehand, according to Tradeweb.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0516 ET - In terms of monetary and fiscal policy, Europe has little room for maneuver to counter a weakening economy, \uc2 UBS\uc2  Chairman \uc2 Axel Weber\uc2  says in an interview with Swiss daily Tages-Anzeiger. Central banks can only take limited countermeasures, he adds. "Italy and France have high deficits, so their hands are tied. Actually, only Germany can counteract this, but that is not enough," the newspaper quotes him as saying. (max.bernhard@dowjones.com; @mxbernhard)\par \par \uc2 0459 ET - The \uc2 ECB\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \uc2 Banca Carige\uc2  put European banking stocks under pressure Wednesday but its impact should be limited since the outcome is predictable, \uc2 Bankinter\uc2  says. The administrators are likely to focus on cleaning up the balance sheet of the bank and trying to find a bigger bank to absorb it, \uc2 Bankinter\uc2  says. Shares in \uc2 Banca Carige\uc2  remain suspended from trading after the \uc2 ECB\uc2  appointed temporary administrators. (pietro.lombardi@dowjones.com; @pietrolombard10)\par \par \uc2 0449 ET - The pound declines slightly after the U.K. purchasing managers' survey on construction activity falls to a three-month low of 52.8 in December, from 53.4 in November, albeit very close to the consensus forecast of 52.9. Sterling edges down to $1.2575, from $1.2585 before the data, while EUR/GBP rises to 0.9048, from 0.9042 beforehand. Sterling had been falling heavily before the data. "U.K. construction firms indicated a disappointing end to 2018 as business activity growth eased to a three-month low and new orders expanded at a relatively subdued pace," the report said. However, "survey respondents cited hopes of a boost to growth from work on big-ticket transport and energy infrastructure projects in 2019." Services \uc2 PMI\uc2 , due Friday, is more important for pound investors given that the U.K. economy is heavily reliant on services. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 03, 2019 09:17 ET (14:17 GMT)\par \par \uc2