\par\par \b \uc2 Step Aside Dollar, Japanese Yen Returns as Safe-Haven Bet -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2019\par 16:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2019, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1030 ET - Last year the dollar rose partly because it was seen as a safe-haven by investors worried about trade relations between the U.S. and China deteriorating. The U.S. economy was growing, whilst China's economy was slowing down, providing another reason why the dollar was a safer bet. However, "without the expectation of higher U.S. rates it is likely that the dollar's safe haven bid will fade this year," says \uc2 Jane Foley\uc2  , senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  . "Traditionally it is the Japanese yen and the Swiss franc which are the market's favoured safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she says. The yen jumped Thursday, sending USD/JPY overnight to a nine-month low of 104.79 on worries that the Chinese economy was worsening, sparked by an earnings warning from \uc2 Apple\uc2 . (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1022 ET - This morning's ADP report shows a healthy US economy and points to potential upside surprise in December payrolls, says \uc2 Andrew Hunter\uc2  of Capital Economics . "The 271,000 surge in the ADP measure of private employment in December provides further evidence that, for all the recent volatility in financial markets, the US economy remains in a healthy shape going into 2019," Hunter says. While the survey is not always a good guide for the non-farm payroll numbers, the firm says the stronger ADP reading in December suggests that tomorrow's employment report could beat expectations. Economists surveyed by the Wall Street Journal are looking for an increase of 176K payrolls, while the unemployment rate is seen ticking down to 3.6%. (francesca.fontana@wsj.com, @francescamarief)\par \par \uc2 1017 ET - U.S. Fed funds futures point out a 91% chance that U.S. interest rates will finish 2019 at or below current levels, which is "a sharp contrast with the outlook implied as recently as November," says \uc2 Jane Foley\uc2  , senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  . "This change in market forecasts regarding the Fed has significant implications for the outlook of USD/JPY," she says. \uc2 Apple\uc2 's revenue warning "is a metaphor for current market anxieties," she adds. \uc2 Apple\uc2  said earnings would come in lower than expected due to poor sales in China, raising concerns about a slowing Chinese economy. Chinese manufacturing \uc2 PMI\uc2  has recently dropped into contraction territory. As result, USD/JPY tumbled overnight to a nine-month low of 104.79 and is last down 1.5% at 107.26. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1017 ET - Treasury yields fall sharply along with stocks and the dollar after a weaker-than-expected manufacturing report. The \uc2 Institute for Supply Management\uc2  said its manufacturing index fell to 54.1 in December from 59.3 in November. Economists surveyed by the Wall Street Journal had expected a reading of 57.9. While readings above 50 indicate activity is expanding across the manufacturing sector, the slowdown should add to concerns about the economy as financial conditions tighten and the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  continues to signal that more interest-rate increases lie ahead. The 10-year yield was recently 2.611% vs. 2.638% before the report and 2.659% Wednesday. The DJIA is off around 550 points and the dollar loses 1.4% against the yen and 0.5% to the euro. (sam.godlfarb@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0953 ET - \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  advises investors to buy into Ireland and Portugal's new government bonds, expected to be launched via syndicated transactions, to grab new issue premiums that are likely to be "decent." January is a seasonally supply-heavy month in the eurozone with a high number of syndicated transactions, and Ireland and Portugal are among the very first countries to do new deals. \uc2 Danske\uc2  's analysts expect the new bonds to offer "decent" new issue premiums. \uc2 Danske\uc2  says the main risk to this trade idea comes from politics, as was the case in 2016, when Portuguese bonds underperformed after a change in government, and in 2018, when Irish bonds underperformed due to uncertainty caused by Brexit. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0915 ET - Treasury yields continue to edge lower along with global stocks. A catalyst this time is \uc2 Apple\uc2 's cut to its sales forecast, a development that feeds into concerns about China since the move was prompted by ebbing iPhone sales in that country. Yields actually fell in after-hours trading Wednesday and have since drifted a bit higher, buoyed in part by a strong ADP private-sector jobs report. The 10-year yield was recently 2.643% vs. 2.659% Wednesday. (sam.goldfarb@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0917 ET - With the Japanese yen suddenly jumping to a nine-month high versus the U.S. dollar overnight on Thursday, implied volatility went up in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Were the yen to rise even further, the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, says \uc2 Neil Mellor\uc2  , senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNY Mellon. "In view of the uncertainty surrounding the health of the Japanese economy, yen strength is hardly consistent with the Bank's mandates. It is therefore perfectly possible that the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  - guided by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  - could consider returning to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Mr. Mellor says. The dollar is last down by 1% at JPY107.75, having fallen to a nine-month low of 104.79. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0904 ET - The dollar is slightly lower after mixed U.S. economic data, with EUR/USD up 0.2% at 1.1361. The ADP report showed that 271,000 jobs were added during December in the private sector, more than the 178,000 projected by a WSJ poll and the 179,000 in November. But there were also 231,000 jobless claims in December, compared with 216,000 in the previous month and more than the 220,000 claims forecast in a WSJ poll. The dollar rose slightly after the ADP report, but then reversed gains and fell before and after the jobless claims report. EUR/USD had traded around 1.1348 before the ADP data. Data from ADP could serve as guidance for Friday's non-farm payrolls, which gives a more overall picture of U.S. employment. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0853 ET - Various \uc2 European Commission\uc2  proposals and an agreement reached between the U.K. and the U.S. late last year are credit positive for U.K.-based airlines, and to a lesser extent to European Airlines, because they will limit no-fly risk in the event of a no-deal Brexit in March 2019, says Jeanine Arnold, senior credit officer at \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Investors Service. U.K.-based airlines including \uc2 British Airways\uc2  --owned by \uc2 International Consolidated Airlines Group\uc2  --, \uc2 easyJet plc\uc2  and European airlines \uc2 Wizz Air Holdings\uc2  , \uc2 Ryanair\uc2  , \uc2 Thomas Cook Group\uc2  and \uc2 Tui AG\uc2  are set to benefit the most as a significant portion of their earnings depend on EU flyover rights and/or direct flights made between the U.K. and the EU , he says. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com; @lorena_rbal)\par \par \uc2 0803 ET - The Brazilian real extended its surge against the greenback amid increasing confidence that President Bolsonaro is serious about market-friendly reform, says Pablo Spyer, from Mirae asset-management. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trading at 3.78 per dollar, stronger than 3.80 yesterday, when it was already advancing after the inauguration earlier this week. Spyer says the first speech by Economy Minister \uc2 Paulo Guedes\uc2  yesterday "corroborated market expectations" or aggressive reform. "The economy has already made an U-turn and is en route to recoup its investment grade," he said. (paulo.trevisani@wsj.com; @ptrevisani)\par \par \uc2 0752 ET - Turkey's lira has retraced much of the ground lost in the overnight flash crash but remains under pressure. It trades 1.6% lower against the dollar and 2.6% lower against the yen--despite data showing that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to ramp up interest rates have brought inflation under control following last year's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. Consumer prices rose 20.3% in December from a year before, still a rapid rate of growth, but marking the second consecutive month in which inflation has fallen. Timothy Ash, economist at \uc2 BlueBay Asset Management\uc2 , tweets that investors are concerned the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cut rates ahead of local elections on March 31, showing that past "policy failings" have saddled the bank with a "credibility gap." (joe.wallace@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0714 ET - The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  's monetary policy is likely to be data-dependent, so the ISM manufacturing index and the ADP private payrolls are likely to be key for the dollar, says \uc2 MUFG\uc2 . "The impact of surprises in the ISM report has diminished...but for surprises in the range of 2-5% the dollar response has remained strong," \uc2 MUFG\uc2  analysts say, adding "this is particularly true for negative surprises." The ADP jobs report has "typically served as a reliable preview" for the employment change data in the nonfarm payrolls report, due Friday. According to a WSJ survey, December ADP is likely to show growth of 178,000 jobs at 1315 GMT, and ISM manufacturing \uc2 PMI\uc2  is likely to come in at 57.9 at 1500 GMT. EUR/USD is flat at 1.1345. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 03, 2019 10:30 ET (15:30 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020190103ef13001sp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
