\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-UPDATE 1-BOJ's Kuroda urges restraint on tariffs, says stable  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  desirable\b0\par\par\uc2 521 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2018\par 19:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Refiles with no changes to text, fixes spelling of byline)\par \par \uc2 * Trump's comments put \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in spotlight\par \par \uc2 * Policymakers fret about impact of trade protectionism\par \par \uc2 * BOJ's monetary easing programme is at a crossroads\par \par \uc2 By Scott Squires\par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, July 21 (Reuters) - Bank of Japan Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  issued a plea on Saturday for leaders of major economies to step back from a tariff war, and said stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were to everyone's benefit.\par \par \uc2 Kuroda spoke on arrival at a meeting of \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  finance leaders, in response to questions on assertions from U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that Europe and China were manipulating their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favour of their economies.\par \par \uc2 "It is most desirable for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move stably and reflect economic fundamentals," Kuroda said. "This is something we have already reached agreement about at Group of 7 and at G20 (level)."\par \par \uc2 Kuroda also sent hoped debate at the G20 would lead to an easing of retaliatory tariff increases between the United States and China.\par \par \uc2 "Trade protectionism poses merits to no one involved. I think restraint will eventually take hold," he said.\par \par \uc2 Trump has broken with precedent in his presidential role in recent days with comments criticising the dollar's strength and the monetary policies of the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  and central banks in China and Europe,\par \par \uc2 He tweeted on Friday that Fed rate hikes were taking away the U.S.' "competitive edge" in exports.\par \par \uc2 Trump's comments have sparked concern that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will become a new battle ground in the simmering trade war.\par \par \uc2 But, arriving in Buenos Aires, U.S. Treasury Secretary \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2  told reporters that Trump was not trying to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 The subject is particularly sensitive for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  because its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , under Kuroda's leadership, has pursued a massive quantitative easing programme to spur inflation.\par \par \uc2 After five years of easing, the BOJ's attempts to push up inflation have produced minimal results. But the yen has steadily weakened, which could lay Japan open to criticism from its trading partners.\par \par \uc2 The United States this month imposed 25 percent tariffs on $34 billion of Chinese goods to lower the U.S. trade deficit, and China quickly retaliated with an increase in tariffs on U.S. goods.\par \par \uc2 Trump has imposed tariffs on imported steel and aluminium, a blow to Japanese exporters, and has also criticised Japan for its trade surplus and the small number of American vehicles it imports.\par \par \uc2 Asked about reports that the BOJ would debate at this month's rate review whether to make its yield curve control (YCC) policy more flexible, Kuroda said: "It's inappropriate to say anything predictive on the outcome of the meeting."\par \par \uc2 Reuters reported that the BOJ, facing stubbornly low inflation, is in unusually active discussions before this month's policy decision, with changes to its interest-rate targets and stock-buying techniques on the table. (Reporting by Scott Squires in Buenos Aires, writing by Stanley White and Leika Kihara in Tokyo; editing by John Stonestreet) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-7-21T18:20:17.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180721ee7l00gih\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
