\par\par \b \uc2 EUR, JPY to Keep Rising Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Efforts: \uc2 MUFG\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2018\par 12:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1146 GMT - The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  , as well as the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  , may try to verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the rise in the euro and the Japanese yen, but neither of these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to stop from increasing as long as investors know that both central banks are buying fewer government bonds, says \uc2 MUFG\uc2 . EUR/USD reached a fresh three-year high overnight, but it trades down 0.2% at 1.2237 on \uc2 ECB\uc2  members' saying the sudden increase in the euro could be of concern for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . USD/JPY is up 0.2% at 110.72 after Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Taro Aso\uc2  said big swings in USD/JPY would be problematic. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 1136 GMT - The potential for Switzerland to hold a referendum on breaking its agreement with the EU regarding free movement of people could be a positive signal for Brexit negotiations and the pound, says \uc2 MUFG\uc2 . "This could mean that the EU slowly becomes more accommodating with the UK on reaching a positive trade deal," it says, adding: "We continue to see ample upside scope for the pound this year on favourable Brexit developments unfolding." Sterling trades steady against the dollar at 1.3793 and firmer versus the euro, with EUR/GBP down 0.3% at 0.8856.(olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 1120 GMT - Markets are nearly pricing in a full 25 basis points increase to the 1% Canadian interest rate when the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  announces a decision at 1500 GMT, and \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  says the question is whether the \uc2 BOC\uc2  will suggest further rate rises for this year or not. Projections for GDP, the output gap, inflation and interest rates are likely to be revised up today, SocGen says. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "issues a hawkish statement today," EUR/CAD is likely to return to 1.51. EUR/CAD trades down 0.1% at 1.5216. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 1115 GMT - BMI Research, a \uc2 Fitch Group\uc2  company, expects Central and Eastern European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue to perform well due to robust economies and rising rate expectations. BMI expects the Polish PLN to continue appreciating against the euro in the coming months. The next major test is likely to come in around the 4.0 long-term resistance level, says BMI, which forecasts PLN3.66 per euro at the end of 2018. It sees the HUF at 310 to the euro in the short term. The \uc2 National Bank of Hungary\uc2  's "dovish" policy will exert downside pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but a strong domestic economy will provide a tailwind, says BMI. It expects the HUF to average 310 to the euro in 2018. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 1104 GMT - If the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  raises the 1% interest rate by 25 basis points and hints at a further rate increase when it announces a decision at 1500 GMT, USD/CAD could break below support at 1.2356, enabling further falls towards 1.22, according to \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  . However, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't as hawkish, then the Canadian dollar could fall, pushing USD/CAD higher. USD/CAD resistance is at 1.2590, SocGen says. Ahead of the meeting, USD/CAD trades up 0.1% at 1.2442. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 1028 GMT - For bond investors, the impact of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's next monetary policy meeting on Jan. 25 will be "asymmetric," according to \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  strategists: the meeting will either be neutral or trigger a sell-off. They don't see any reasons for the \uc2 ECB\uc2  to support market sentiment by making dovish statements, unless this happens "by accident." And given the risk of a sell-off, it's worth staying short, the strategists say. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 1022 GMT - CreditSights flags two factors that could drive new euro corporate bond supply this year: front-loading issuance ahead of September and expectations of solid economic growth. The credit research firm expects the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to end its net asset purchases in September, which could incentivize some companies to print bonds earlier and take advantage of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid. Meanwhile, eurozone growth may prompt some firms to "buy in revenues" via acquisitions, leading to new bond issuance to finance M&A deals.(tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 1016 GMT - Czech markets shrug off "completely" politics and focus on the economy, say \uc2 KBC Bank\uc2  analysts after the Czech parliament rejected an attempt by Prime Minister Andrej Babis , who faces fraud charges, to form a government. "Actually, the Czech koruna has been extending its gains on rising bets that the \uc2 Czech National Bank\uc2  will deliver another rate hike in early February," the analysts say. \uc2 KBC\uc2  expects the \uc2 Czech National Bank\uc2  to increase its repo rate by 25 basis points on Feb. 1. EUR/CZK last trades up 0.1% at 25.45, having fallen as low as 25.40. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 1008 GMT - The seven-year maturity segment might be the main beneficiary of an anticipated decline in the issuance of ultra-long government bonds in the eurozone this year, say \uc2 Natixis\uc2  rates strategists Cyril Regnat and Jean-Christophe Machado. While it's more than likely that European treasuries will remain very active with issuance in 10-year and longer maturities in 2018, issuance in the 30- to 50-year segment could decline to benefit the seven-year segment, they say. "On the other hand, treasuries are likely to remain very active from 15 to 20 years, given that demand coming from real money investors will remain strong for as long as yields for core and soft core sovereigns camp on low." (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 1005 GMT - \uc2 Barclays\uc2  nudges up its 2018 headline U.K. CPI forecast, expecting it to average 2.6% this year versus its previous assumption of 2.5%, citing slightly stronger oil price assumptions. But when the energy base effect wanes in 2019, average inflation should decrease to 2.2%. Meanwhile, forecasts on core inflation--which includes volatile components--are unchanged. Headline inflation is a closely tracked indicator among U.K. bond investors, not least because it can affect the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  's monetary policy decisions. The \uc2 BOE\uc2  has a mandated inflation target of 2%. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0952 GMT - The bonds of \uc2 Verbund\uc2  look set to gain from the Austrian electricity firm's increased guidance for 2017, according to \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  analyst Michael Gerstner. \uc2 Verbund\uc2  now expects Ebitda of around EUR920 million versus the previous forecast of around EUR830 million. Meanwhile, the 40% dividend payout ratio for 2017 is "still conservative" compared to European peers and justified by strong operating performance in recent quarters, Mr. Gerstner adds. Bond dealers are yet to alter their quotes on \uc2 Verbund\uc2  issues early Wednesday. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0952 GMT - Conflicting economic data leaves a few options for \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  at its interest rate decision, due 1500 GMT, says BK Asset Management. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can increase the rate by 25 basis points and "downplay the move by suggesting future hikes are data dependent." Or it could hold the 1% rate, but "acknowledge improvements in the economy and signal plans to tighten in March." Either way, CAD is likely to return to current levels. USD/CAD trades up 0.2% at 1.2456. In the first scenario USD/CAD will fall to 1.24/1.2350 but "recover quickly." In the second, it will rise to 1.25 but "retreat aggressively," BK says. Only a rise with signals of more to come, would see the Canadian dollar rise significantly, taking USD/CAD to 1.23. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 17, 2018 06:46 ET (11:46 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180117ee1h00147\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\a